#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai.rst:6
msgid "AI"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai.rst:8
msgid "The **AI** application is eYssen's security-first LLM assistant for Odoo. It connects your database to language-model providers (OpenAI, Anthropic, xAI, Google Gemini, OpenRouter and compatible APIs), lets users chat with a grounded assistant about *this* Odoo instance, and can run **autonomous agents** that act as narrow-privilege colleagues on Discuss, chatter, activities and project tasks."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai.rst:15
msgid "Every data operation the model requests goes through a single access gate: the assistant never receives more privilege than the user (or the agent user) already holds in Odoo, and an admin can narrow that further with AI access policies, capabilities, channel rules and write confirmation."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai.rst:21
msgid "**Misconfigured AI is dangerous.** An AI agent with broad Odoo groups, open write capabilities, or ``agent_full`` channel scope can read, change or delete business data, send content to an external LLM provider, and act unattended. Read :doc:`ai/security` **before** enabling write capabilities, linking agent users, or exposing AI to untrusted requesters. Default install is read-oriented and write-denied; every privilege you add is a deliberate decision."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai.rst:29
msgid "The technical module name is ``ai`` (Productivity / AI). It depends on **Mail**, **Web**, **Project**, and eYssen's project template/category helpers used for the AI Ops work queue."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai.rst:34
msgid "What you can do"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai.rst:36
msgid "**Interactive assistant** — systray chat bubble and :menuselection:`AI --> Conversations` for grounded Q&A, schema search, optional web fetch, file ingest, skills and memory."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai.rst:39
msgid "**Human-confirmed writes** — create/update/delete proposals in :menuselection:`AI --> Write Proposals` instead of silent mutations (configurable)."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai.rst:41
msgid "**Autonomous agents** — optional linked ``res.users`` identities with a supervisor, channel allow-lists, capability ceilings, per-task write mode (confirm by default; hybrid/auto only as an explicit opt-in), pending-write approval with a systray nudge on the **business record**, and supervisor-requested cancellation (see :doc:`ai/agents`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai.rst:46
msgid "**Access policy framework** — per-group / per-model / per-field allow·deny on top of Odoo ACLs (never grants beyond the acting user's own rights)."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai.rst:48
msgid "**Skills** — reusable instruction packs (factory + custom) activated always or on demand."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai.rst:50
msgid "**Memory** — durable user/agent/company memories with graph and search tools."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai.rst:51
msgid "**Monitoring** — audit logs, violation strikes, temporary bans, and an agent run ledger in which a run whose worker died is closed automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai.rst:53
msgid "**Optional MCP / web / UI customization** — external tools, web search, and admin-only schema/view customization, all capability-gated and off by default where risky."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai.rst:56
msgid "**Everyday help in the forms you use** — a writing assistant in editors and chatter, an AI search bar, a command palette, AI-filled fields and AI in server actions and automations (see :doc:`ai/writing_assistant`, :doc:`ai/search_and_commands` and :doc:`ai/fields_and_automation`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai.rst:60
msgid "**Knowledge sources** — answers with citations from files, web pages, records, Knowledge articles and Documents (see :doc:`ai/knowledge_sources` and :doc:`ai/knowledge_documents`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai.rst:63
msgid "**MCP server** — connect Claude, ChatGPT or another AI app to your database with OAuth sign-in and per-user consent (see :doc:`ai/mcp_server`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai.rst:65
msgid "**Website and live chat** — an AI agent that answers website visitors with a hand-over to your operators, an AI page generator, builder tools and brand kits (see :doc:`ai/livechat` and :doc:`ai/website`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai.rst:68
msgid "**Voice** — dictate messages and have Discuss calls transcribed and summarised, with consent from each participant (see :doc:`ai/voice`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai.rst:70
msgid "**Business apps** — quick prompts and buttons in CRM, Sales, Purchase, Inventory, Manufacturing, Invoicing, Calendar, Products, Email marketing and Timesheets, ticket triage for projects with SLA and AI analysis of accounting reports (see :doc:`ai/app_integrations`, :doc:`ai/project_sla` and :doc:`ai/accounting_reports`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai.rst:75
msgid "**CAD imports** — suggested quantities and lengths for the members of a steel structure drawing, which you accept or reject (see :doc:`ai/cad_bom_import`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai.rst:77
msgid "**Providers, models and access** — chat, image, embedding and speech-to-text models, and a clear overview of who can use which AI feature (see :doc:`ai/models_and_providers`, :doc:`ai/panel` and :doc:`ai/feature_access`)."
