#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/access_policy.rst:249
msgid "Prefer a dedicated free-busy API/action if you add one later; raw event read is a common over-share."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/access_policy.rst:251
msgid "``perm_create`` = Allow with write-allow only on start, stop, name (generic), user_id."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/access_policy.rst:254
msgid "See :doc:`agent_recipes` for end-to-end agent recipes that combine policy, capabilities and channels."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/access_policy.rst:258
msgid "Relation to Odoo record rules"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/access_policy.rst:260
msgid "AI policy does **not** replace record rules. Multi-company, follower-only documents, and portal isolation remain enforced by Odoo when the gate runs as the user. When designing \"create but not read\", verify both layers: a create that returns a read snapshot may still fail or strip if read is denied — the assistant should treat tool errors as authoritative."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/accounting_reports.rst:3
msgid "AI for accounting reports"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/accounting_reports.rst:5
msgid "The module AI for Accounting Reports adds an assistant to the financial reports. It explains a report in plain language, points out trends and anomalies, and can run a second, independent check of its own findings with two AI agents. It never changes any accounting data."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/accounting_reports.rst:11
msgid "Analyse a report"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/accounting_reports.rst:13
msgid "Open a report wizard, for example profit and loss, balance sheet, trial balance, general ledger, partner ledger, aged partner balance, tax report or journal audit, and set the dates and options as you normally would."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/accounting_reports.rst:16
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Analyse with AI` next to the usual print button (accountants only). You land on a new analysis. The analysis runs in the background; the form shows its progress and you are notified when it is done."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/accounting_reports.rst:19
msgid "Read the result on the tab :guilabel:`Analysis`. The tab :guilabel:`Report data` shows the rows the AI was given. Use :guilabel:`Analyse again` to run it again."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/accounting_reports.rst:23
msgid "All analyses are listed in :menuselection:`Accounting --> Reporting --> AI Report Analyses`. You see your own analyses; accounting managers see those of the company. Each analysis has its own chatter."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/accounting_reports.rst:28
msgid "What the AI is given"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/accounting_reports.rst:30
msgid "The AI works from the report's own computed rows, the same figures you could print, calculated in your environment with your access rights. No PDF is read. Each row gets a reference (R1, R2, and so on) so that findings can point to their evidence."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/accounting_reports.rst:34
msgid "For financial reports and the trial balance with two dates and no comparison chosen, the same report is also computed for the previous period of the same length, so the AI can describe trends."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/accounting_reports.rst:37
msgid "Key figures such as current ratio, quick ratio, debt to equity, margins, net result and income growth are calculated by the program, not by the AI. The AI only explains them. They are approximations from the account lines of the report, and a report without account detail gives none."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/accounting_reports.rst:41
msgid "A report is limited to 400 rows. A large general ledger is reduced to account totals plus the 25 largest items of the period, and the text given to the AI is capped."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/accounting_reports.rst:46
msgid "Audit with an auditor and a reviewer"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/accounting_reports.rst:48
msgid "On an analysis, click :guilabel:`Audit with AI agents` for a more careful check. It also runs in the background."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/accounting_reports.rst:51
msgid "The agent :guilabel:`Financial Auditor` proposes up to eight findings, each citing the report rows as evidence and, where relevant, an amount."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/accounting_reports.rst:53
msgid "It hands them to a second agent, :guilabel:`Financial Reviewer`, which looks the rows up and confirms or rejects every finding."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/accounting_reports.rst:55
msgid "The program then checks the evidence itself: a finding stays :guilabel:`Confirmed` only if the reviewer confirmed it, every row it cites exists and its amount (if any) is found in the cited rows within 0.5 percent. Findings that were not reviewed or are not supported are kept as rejected, with the reason, so nothing is hidden."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/accounting_reports.rst:61
msgid "The result is the tab :guilabel:`Audit` with a summary, the :guilabel:`Confirmed findings` and the :guilabel:`Rejected findings` with their severity, evidence and verdict, plus a note in the chatter that lists the confirmed findings. Click :guilabel:`Open audit in AI panel` to read or continue the conversation with the auditor in the AI panel (see :doc:`panel`). The panel can also look up the report rows while the analysis is open, and two quick prompts are offered: :guilabel:`Explain this report` and :guilabel:`What should I check first?`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/accounting_reports.rst:70
msgid "Safety and requirements"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/accounting_reports.rst:72
msgid "Read-only: the two agents have only the Ask capability and no tools that read or write records. The only things written are the analysis and its findings, the AI conversation and the logs. Journal entries and other accounting data stay unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/accounting_reports.rst:76
msgid "Before anything is sent, the program checks that a model is configured, that you have the Ask and Read capabilities, and that the AI read policy allows journal items and accounts (see :doc:`access_policy`). If not, you get a plain message and no strike is recorded."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/accounting_reports.rst:80
msgid "The agents are available to accountants only. Their names are translatable, so they follow the language of the user."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/accounting_reports.rst:82
msgid "Reports of the optional cash book, bank book and day book modules have their own wizards and are not covered."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/accounting_reports.rst:86
msgid "Note for administrators: background jobs and time limits"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/accounting_reports.rst:88
msgid "An audit makes several model calls and easily takes longer than an ordinary web request is allowed to run. That is why analyses and audits run as background jobs of the scheduled action \"AI: Run accounting report analyses and audits\". The job runs in the environment of the person who clicked, never in the identity of the scheduler, and the form refreshes by itself. A job that stays in the running state for more than 30 minutes is marked as failed with the message \"The AI job was interrupted. Start it again.\", so nothing stays stuck."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/accounting_reports.rst:97
msgid "The time a background job may run comes from the server option ``limit_time_real_cron`` when it is set to a positive value, otherwise from ``limit_time_real``, and otherwise from Odoo's default. If audits fail with a timeout, raise ``limit_time_real_cron`` in the server configuration file (for example to 900 seconds) and restart the server. The value 0 is not treated as \"no limit\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/accounting_reports.rst:104
msgid "If the model does not answer within the time that is left, the analysis or audit ends as failed with the message \"The AI model did not answer in time. Try again later, or ask for something shorter or narrower.\" The message is shown on the analysis, posted in its chatter and sent to you as a notification."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/agent_recipes.rst:3
msgid "Agent recipes"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/agent_recipes.rst:5
msgid "This page shows **how to combine** Odoo groups, AI capabilities, access policies and channel rules for common roles. Adjust model names to the apps you actually install (Helpdesk vs Project, Appointment vs Calendar, …)."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/agent_recipes.rst:10
msgid "Every recipe assumes you read :doc:`security` first. Copying a recipe without matching Odoo ACLs on the agent user will either fail closed or — if you over-grant Odoo groups — fail **open**."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/agent_recipes.rst:15
msgid "Recipe checklist (all agents)"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/agent_recipes.rst:17
msgid "Create a **dedicated** internal user (no password login needed for pure cron/agent use if your SSO policy allows; **no API keys**)."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/agent_recipes.rst:19
msgid "Give that user **only** the Odoo groups required for the business objects."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/agent_recipes.rst:20
msgid "Create an AI access group containing that user; add **deny** rules for everything sensitive outside the mission."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/agent_recipes.rst:22
msgid "Check whether the mission needs to write a field that also writes another model — a vendor bill's partner or journal, an invoice line's product, a lead's email. Those need a rule naming the **field**; a model-level Allow deliberately does not open them. See :ref:`ai/policy/cross-model`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/agent_recipes.rst:26
msgid "Create ``ai.agent``: link user, supervisor, capability_ids, system prompt."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/agent_recipes.rst:27
