#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/app_integrations.rst:5
msgid "For many eYssen apps there is a small AI module that adds quick prompts and a few buttons to the forms you already use. The modules install themselves when the AI module and the matching app are both installed, so there is nothing to set up beyond the normal AI configuration (see :doc:`getting_started`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/app_integrations.rst:11
msgid "How they work"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/app_integrations.rst:13
msgid "Quick prompts appear as chips in the AI panel when a record of the app is open in a form view (see :doc:`panel`). Administrators can edit or archive them like any other quick prompt."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/app_integrations.rst:16
msgid "The AI reads only what you may see: your access rights, record rules and the AI access rules all apply (see :doc:`access_policy`). If an access rule stops the AI from reading what a button needs, you get a clear message instead of a partial result."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/app_integrations.rst:20
msgid "Buttons that change data work as your own decision: the AI proposes values, you click, and the change is made with your rights and recorded in the AI change log (see :doc:`monitoring`). Buttons that only draft text never send or save anything on their own."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/app_integrations.rst:24
msgid "Texts found in records, messages and descriptions are treated as untrusted content: the AI is told never to follow instructions written inside them."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/app_integrations.rst:28
msgid "CRM"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/app_integrations.rst:30
msgid "On a lead or opportunity the quick prompts are :guilabel:`Qualify` (a short assessment of the lead and of the information that is still missing), :guilabel:`Next best action` and :guilabel:`Follow-up email`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/app_integrations.rst:34
msgid "The button :guilabel:`Assign with AI` in the form header (and in the action menu of the list, for up to 20 leads at a time) picks a salesperson and a sales team for each lead. The AI looks at the lead, the sales teams and their members, the open workload of each salesperson and how many leads each of them won in the last year, in total and in the lead's country. It can only choose from the people and teams it was offered. The assignment is written with your rights, and a note \"Assigned with AI\" with the reason is added to the chatter. Leads you cannot edit are skipped, and a summary tells you how many were assigned and why others were not."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/app_integrations.rst:45
msgid "Sales, Purchase and Inventory"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/app_integrations.rst:47
msgid "Sales orders: :guilabel:`Summarise`, :guilabel:`Upsell ideas` (from the customer's order history) and :guilabel:`Follow-up`. When the margin or the delivery apps are installed, :guilabel:`Margin check` and :guilabel:`Delivery status` are added as well. If an administrator deletes one of them, it does not come back."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/app_integrations.rst:52
msgid "Purchase orders: :guilabel:`Compare with previous purchases` (price, vendor and lead time for the same products), :guilabel:`RFQ reminder` (a reminder to the vendor) and :guilabel:`Summarise`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/app_integrations.rst:55
msgid "Transfers: :guilabel:`Explain delays` and :guilabel:`Stock risk`. Products and product variants also have :guilabel:`Stock risk`, which compares the stock on hand with the forecast and the open demand. These are shown to Inventory users."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/app_integrations.rst:59
msgid "On an open product or variant, the AI is given the stock figures of the record: quantity on hand, forecasted and free quantity, incoming and outgoing quantities and the limits of the reordering rules. They are read with your rights, like the rest of the record, so the assistant does not have to guess where they are. For the open transfers behind them it searches the stock moves."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/app_integrations.rst:67
msgid "Manufacturing"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/app_integrations.rst:69
