msgid "Acting identity on apply"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/using_the_assistant.rst:112
msgid "The chat user"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/using_the_assistant.rst:112
msgid "The **agent user** (from the run), not the supervisor"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/using_the_assistant.rst:115
msgid "Systray nudge"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/using_the_assistant.rst:115
msgid "Chat card / own proposals list"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/using_the_assistant.rst:115
msgid "To-Do on the **business record** when possible, else on the task"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/using_the_assistant.rst:120
msgid "The agent lifetime applies only while the proposing run is still open. Once that run has ended — :guilabel:`Done`, :guilabel:`Failed` or :guilabel:`Timed out` — the **AI: Expire pending writes** scheduled action expires its remaining proposals on its next pass, at most 15 minutes later, whatever the lifetime says. The case that catches supervisors out is a run that overran its own time limit: it closes as :guilabel:`Timed out` while still holding open proposals. Review proposals from failed and timed-out runs promptly. If you open a :guilabel:`To-Do` for a proposal that no longer exists, mark the activity done: the proposal expired with its run."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/using_the_assistant.rst:131
msgid "Approving an agent proposal means: \"I authorise this agent to perform this change with *its* rights.\" The supervisor does not need (and should not use) broader rights than necessary to review the summary — execution rights come from the agent user + policy at apply time."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/using_the_assistant.rst:137
msgid "Write modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/using_the_assistant.rst:139
msgid "**Interactive chat** — under :menuselection:`AI --> Configuration --> Settings`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/using_the_assistant.rst:141
msgid "**Apply automatically** — every create/write/delete/file tool runs immediately. Highest risk."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/using_the_assistant.rst:143
msgid "**Always require confirmation** — everything becomes a proposal."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/using_the_assistant.rst:144
msgid "**Create automatically, confirm updates** (*hybrid*, default) — only *new* records auto-apply; updates, deletes and file attaches wait for confirmation."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/using_the_assistant.rst:147
msgid "**Agent runs** — same three values, but on the **task** form (:guilabel:`Write Mode`), defaulting to *Always require confirmation*. The Settings value does not apply to agent runs. Use *auto* or *hybrid* only when the standing instruction and skills keep risk bounded (draft-only fills, no posting, no payments). Details: :ref:`ai/agents/task-write-mode`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/using_the_assistant.rst:153
msgid "A TTL of 0 disables expiry **by age** for that class of proposals. It does not disable the sweep described above: a proposal whose agent run has already ended is expired however long you are prepared to wait for an approval."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/using_the_assistant.rst:158
msgid "Navigating the UI"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/using_the_assistant.rst:160
msgid "With the **Navigate** capability, the assistant can help open menus / actions the user is allowed to reach. It does not bypass menu ACLs."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/using_the_assistant.rst:164
msgid "Presenting choices"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/using_the_assistant.rst:166
msgid "The assistant may use a structured **present choices** tool so the UI can show selectable options instead of free text only (when supported by the chat frontend)."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/using_the_assistant.rst:171
msgid "What the assistant should not do"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/using_the_assistant.rst:173
msgid "Claim a model, field, stage or module exists without tool or environment evidence on *this* database."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/using_the_assistant.rst:175
msgid "Write ``state`` directly to skip business buttons."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/using_the_assistant.rst:176
msgid "Promise that an email was sent to a customer unless a real mail tool/action did so under policy (shipped support prompts forbid fake send claims)."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/using_the_assistant.rst:178
msgid "Treat ticket text as a privilege upgrade."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/using_the_assistant.rst:180
msgid "For agent-driven work (assignment, @mention), see :doc:`agents`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/voice.rst:3
msgid "Voice: dictation and call transcription"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/voice.rst:5
msgid "The module AI Voice adds speech to text to eYssen. You can dictate messages instead of typing them, and you can have a Discuss call transcribed and summarised, with action items. It uses a speech-to-text model that an administrator configures once."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/voice.rst:11
msgid "Set up speech to text"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/voice.rst:13
msgid "Add a provider that offers the OpenAI-compatible transcription route, for example OpenAI, or Groq or a self-hosted Whisper server using the provider type OpenAI with its own base URL (see :doc:`models_and_providers`). Anthropic and OpenRouter have no transcription route and cannot be used for speech to text."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/voice.rst:18
msgid "Refresh the models of the provider. Ids that contain ``whisper`` or ``transcribe`` are classified as :guilabel:`Speech to text` models automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/voice.rst:21
msgid "Open :menuselection:`AI --> Configuration --> Settings`, find the block :guilabel:`Voice` and choose the :guilabel:`Speech-to-text model`. Dictation and call transcription stay hidden until a model is chosen."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/voice.rst:25
msgid "The other settings of the block are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/voice.rst:27
msgid ":guilabel:`Spoken language`: an optional two-letter language code such as ``hu`` or ``es``. Leave it empty to detect the language automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/voice.rst:29
msgid ":guilabel:`Max recording size (MB)`: the limit per uploaded recording or call piece (10 MB by default, never more than 25 MB)."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/voice.rst:31
msgid ":guilabel:`Max dictation length (seconds)`: a dictation stops by itself after this time (120 seconds by default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/voice.rst:33
msgid ":guilabel:`Call chunk length (seconds)`: call audio is uploaded and transcribed in pieces of this length (30 seconds by default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/voice.rst:35
msgid ":guilabel:`Max transcribed minutes per call and person` (180 by default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/voice.rst:36
msgid ":guilabel:`Keep call audio (days)`: how long the call recordings are kept (7 days by default). With 0 the audio is not stored at all, only the text. The text always stays."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/voice.rst:39
msgid ":guilabel:`Summarize calls automatically`: when a transcribed call ends, a summary with action items is posted in the channel (on by default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/voice.rst:43
msgid "Speech to text uses the AI capability Ask, the same rate limits as other AI requests and the daily call and cost caps. Each request is written to the AI log, with its cost estimated from the audio length or the token usage."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/voice.rst:48
msgid "Dictate instead of typing"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/voice.rst:50
msgid "A microphone button (:guilabel:`Dictate`) appears in the message box of the chatter and of Discuss, also when you edit a message, and next to the input of the AI panel. It is shown only to AI users, once a speech-to-text model is configured and when your browser can record."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/voice.rst:55
msgid "Click the microphone and allow the browser to use it when asked."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/voice.rst:56
msgid "Speak. Click the button again (:guilabel:`Stop dictation`) when you are done, or wait for the maximum length."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/voice.rst:58
msgid "The recognised text is inserted at the cursor. It is never sent automatically: read it, correct it and send it with the normal button."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/voice.rst:61
msgid "The dictation audio is sent to the provider for transcription and is never stored in eYssen."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/voice.rst:65
msgid "Transcribe a call"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/voice.rst:67
msgid "In a Discuss call, every participant sees the action :guilabel:`Transcribe` in the call controls (or :guilabel:`Join transcription` once someone has started it, and :guilabel:`Stop transcription` while you take part). While a call is being transcribed, the action is highlighted for everyone."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/voice.rst:73
msgid "How consent works"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/voice.rst:75
msgid "Transcription is opt-in for each person:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/voice.rst:77
msgid "Turning it on asks you to confirm that your microphone will be recorded and transcribed."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/voice.rst:79
msgid "When the first participant starts the transcription, a notice is posted in the channel. It says who started it, that only people who turn it on themselves are recorded, each from their own microphone, and how long the audio is kept. Everyone who joins later is announced the same way."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/voice.rst:83
msgid "Each browser records only its own microphone, and only while that person has it turned on and is not muted. The server refuses audio from people who did not opt in and from people outside the channel."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/voice.rst:86
msgid "Turning it off, leaving the call or the end of the call stops your recording. Guests who are not users cannot take part."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/voice.rst:90
msgid "Check the privacy and employment rules that apply to you before you use call transcription, and tell the people on your calls. The audio is sent to the speech-to-text provider you configured."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/voice.rst:95
msgid "Transcript, summary and action items"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/voice.rst:97
msgid "When the last person turns transcription off, or nobody is left in the call, the transcript ends. If :guilabel:`Summarize calls automatically` is on, a summary is posted in the channel about a minute later, as a comment from the person who started the transcription. It contains the summary, the action items with a suggested person and a link to the transcript."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/voice.rst:103
msgid "Open all transcripts in :menuselection:`AI --> Call transcripts`. Members of the channel see their own calls; AI administrators see all of them. On a transcript you have the tabs :guilabel:`Summary` and :guilabel:`Transcript`, the list of :guilabel:`Action items` and the buttons :guilabel:`Summarize` or :guilabel:`Summarize again` if you want a summary on demand (not while the call is still being recorded). Filter the list with :guilabel:`I took part` and :guilabel:`Not summarized`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/voice.rst:111
msgid "The AI only suggests an assignee when the name spoken in the call matches exactly one internal member of the channel. Nothing is scheduled automatically: review the items on the transcript, edit the task, person or due date, tick the ones you want and click :guilabel:`Create activities`. Your click is the confirmation. Every item with an assignee gets a To-Do activity; the assignee must be a channel member."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/voice.rst:121
msgid "Words spoken across the boundary of two pieces of audio can be split, and a single browser records one speaker only."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/voice.rst:123
msgid "Very long calls are summarised from the last 60,000 characters of the transcript."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/voice.rst:125
msgid "The push-to-talk and voice-activation settings of the call are not mirrored; only the mute state is respected."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/website.rst:3
msgid "Website AI"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/website.rst:5
msgid "The module AI Website adds three things to the eYssen website builder: a page generator, builder tools for the AI panel and brand kits. All of them are for website designers, and the AI never writes raw HTML or scripts: it only chooses and fills your website's own building blocks."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/website.rst:11
msgid "Page generator"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/website.rst:13
msgid "The generator turns a short brief into a complete page. You can start it in two places:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/website.rst:16
msgid "In the website editor, click :guilabel:`New` and choose :guilabel:`Page with AI`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/website.rst:18
msgid "In the backend, open :menuselection:`Website --> Site --> Create a page with AI`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/website.rst:21
msgid "Fill in the brief:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/website.rst:23
msgid ":guilabel:`Page name`, :guilabel:`What is the page for?` and, optionally, the :guilabel:`Audience`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/website.rst:25
msgid ":guilabel:`Sections to include`: the sections you want, in order, one per line."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/website.rst:27
msgid ":guilabel:`Tone` (:guilabel:`Professional`, :guilabel:`Friendly`, :guilabel:`Enthusiastic`, :guilabel:`Formal`, :guilabel:`Playful` or :guilabel:`Short and to the point`) and :guilabel:`Language`, chosen among the installed languages."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/website.rst:31
msgid ":guilabel:`Add to the menu` adds a menu item for the new page. :guilabel:`Search pictures on Unsplash` appears only when an Unsplash key is configured; without it the blocks keep their default pictures, which you can replace in the editor."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/website.rst:36
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Generate page`. The page is created unpublished and opens in the editor, so you can review and adjust it before publishing. Clicking the button is the confirmation, so no extra approval card appears."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/website.rst:41
msgid "The generator can use twelve common building blocks: cover, title, text, text with image, image with text, picture, three columns, features, numbers, call to action, FAQ and contact information. Blocks added by a theme are not offered, but a theme's own version of a listed block is used. The contact block takes the e-mail address, phone number and address from your company. Texts are plain text and the AI is told not to invent prices, figures, quotes or names, so always review the page."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/website.rst:50
msgid "Builder tools in the AI panel"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/website.rst:52
msgid "Website designers who have the :guilabel:`Customize UI & schema` capability can also ask the AI panel (see :doc:`panel`) to work on the website. That capability is off by default and for administrators only (see :doc:`feature_access`). The AI bubble is in the top bar of the website preview too, so you can open the panel while you look at the page. The shipped agent :guilabel:`Website builder` is set up for this: it first looks at the existing pages and menus, proposes changes and never says that something is done before you confirm it."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/website.rst:60
msgid "The tools can:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/website.rst:62
msgid "list the usable blocks, pages, menu items and brand kits;"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/website.rst:63
msgid "create a new unpublished page from a plan of blocks, optionally with a menu item;"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/website.rst:65
msgid "insert one block at the start, at the end or at a given position of a page;"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/website.rst:66
msgid "add, rename and reorder menu items;"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/website.rst:67
msgid "replace or append a block of custom CSS managed by the AI;"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/website.rst:68
msgid "apply a saved brand kit, or colours and fonts you give."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/website.rst:71
msgid "Confirmation cards"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/website.rst:73
msgid "Website changes are public, so they are always proposed first: the panel shows a card that you confirm or cancel (see :doc:`panel`). Only the :guilabel:`Apply without asking` write mode applies them straight away; the mixed mode still asks. The card shows the full content of the change, not a summary: every block with its title, texts, buttons and their targets, the replaced links, a note when a block goes onto an already published page and, for CSS changes, the complete CSS. A link to another website is marked on the card with the host it leads to. The change is checked again when you confirm."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/website.rst:83
msgid "Links and CSS rules"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/website.rst:85
msgid "Links. The builder links only to pages and anchors that exist on this website, to its own absolute addresses, to e-mail addresses and to phone numbers. A made-up path or a link to another website is replaced and listed on the card; a menu item that points to another website is refused. An administrator can lift this with :guilabel:`AI may add links to other websites` in the block :guilabel:`Website builder` of :menuselection:`AI --> Configuration --> Settings`. Such links are then still marked on the card."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/website.rst:92
msgid "Custom CSS. The AI may only write plain CSS rules between its own markers in the website's custom stylesheet; your own rules outside the markers are kept. Sass is refused (variables, interpolation and the like), as are imports, scripts, functions that CSS does not know and at-rules other than ``@media``, ``@supports``, ``@keyframes`` and ``@font-face``. An ``url()`` may only point to pictures and static files of this site. The CSS is compiled once on its own and the result is checked again, and then the website's real frontend style bundle is compiled with the new rules before anything is saved. If it does not compile, nothing is saved and the error is shown."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/website.rst:102
msgid "If a turn has no builder tools (the capability is missing or you are not a website designer), the assistant tells you that the :guilabel:`Customize UI & schema` capability or the website designer right is missing, that an administrator can grant it, and explains the manual way instead: Menu Editor, Pages, edit mode and theme settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/website.rst:109
msgid "Brand kits"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/website.rst:111
msgid "A brand kit keeps your brand colours, fonts and logo together. Open :menuselection:`Website --> Configuration --> Brand kits`, click New and fill in a name, optionally a website (leave it empty to use the kit on any website), the five colours (:guilabel:`Primary colour`, :guilabel:`Secondary colour`, :guilabel:`Accent colour`, :guilabel:`Light colour`, :guilabel:`Dark colour`) as ``#RRGGBB`` values, the :guilabel:`Text font` and :guilabel:`Headings font`, and the logo. Empty values are left unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/website.rst:119
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Apply to the website` to set the colour palette, the fonts and the logo of the website theme in one step, exactly as the Theme tab of the editor would. A font that the website does not ship is loaded from Google Fonts. The AI panel can do the same with the tool for brand kits."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/website.rst:125
msgid "Who can use it"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/website.rst:127
msgid "The page generator and the brand kits need the website designer access right. Builder tools in the AI panel need the website designer right and the customize capability."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/website.rst:130
msgid "Public visitors, portal users and the live chat agent never see the builder tools."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/website.rst:132
msgid "If an AI access rule denies the website models, the builder is blocked as well (see :doc:`access_policy`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/website.rst:136
msgid "The preview cards that the live chat agent can show to visitors are described in :doc:`livechat`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/writing_assistant.rst:3
msgid "Writing assistant"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/writing_assistant.rst:5
msgid "The writing assistant helps you write texts where you already work: in any rich-text field, in the chatter of a record and in the image dialog of the editor. It only produces text or a picture for you to review. Nothing is posted, sent or saved until you do it yourself."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/writing_assistant.rst:10
msgid "It needs a chat model (and, for pictures, an image model) set under :menuselection:`AI --> Configuration --> Settings`, and your user must be in the :guilabel:`AI: User` group. Every request counts against your rate limit and is written to the AI log."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/writing_assistant.rst:16
msgid "AI writer in the editor"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/writing_assistant.rst:18
msgid "In any rich-text field (a description, a note, an email body), type ``/`` and choose :guilabel:`AI writer` under the AI tools. You can also select some text and click the :guilabel:`AI` button in the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/writing_assistant.rst:21
msgid "In the dialog :guilabel:`Generate text with AI`, say what you want: write a paragraph, rewrite the selection in a friendlier tone, shorten it, expand it, fix the grammar or translate it. The dialog keeps the conversation, so you can refine the result with follow-up messages."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/writing_assistant.rst:25
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Insert` on the answer you like. It replaces the selection or goes at the cursor. If you do not like it, close the dialog: the document is unchanged."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/writing_assistant.rst:29
msgid "To translate selected text quickly, use the :guilabel:`Translate with AI` language selector in the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/writing_assistant.rst:33
msgid "The same dialog is used in the email marketing editor (see :doc:`app_integrations`), where it is also called :guilabel:`AI writer`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/writing_assistant.rst:37
msgid "Draft with AI in the chatter"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/writing_assistant.rst:39
msgid "On a saved record, the message composer of the chatter shows a :guilabel:`Draft with AI` button (a magic wand next to the attachment button). Use it for both a reply to followers (:guilabel:`Send message`) and an internal note. The assistant reads the record and its recent messages and writes a draft into the box. If you had already typed something, it takes your text into account."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/writing_assistant.rst:45
msgid "The draft is only placed in the box. Edit it and send it the usual way. The button is not offered in Discuss channels or while you are editing an existing message."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/writing_assistant.rst:50
msgid "AI images in the media dialog"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/writing_assistant.rst:52
msgid "When an image model is configured, the editor's media dialog (the picture button, or the ``/image`` command) gets an :guilabel:`AI image` tab. Describe the picture in :guilabel:`Describe the image`, choose :guilabel:`Landscape`, :guilabel:`Square` or :guilabel:`Portrait`, and click :guilabel:`Generate`. When the preview looks right, add it like any uploaded picture. It is stored as a normal attachment."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/writing_assistant.rst:60
msgid "Good to know"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/writing_assistant.rst:62
msgid "Review before you use: the model can be wrong, and the text it writes is yours once you insert or send it."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/writing_assistant.rst:64
msgid "The assistant only sees what you may see. The chatter draft reads the record and its thread with your own rights; if an administrator denied the AI access to that model, the draft is written from the conversation alone."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/ai/writing_assistant.rst:67
msgid "Prompts are sent to your AI provider. Do not paste secrets or data you may not share with it."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:5
msgid "Appointments"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:12
msgid "The **Appointments** app lets customers and colleagues book time with the company: an *appointment type* defines who can be booked, when, for how long, and under which conditions, and each booking creates a calendar event for the provider."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:17
msgid "The app is provided by the eYssen *Appointment* module family (``appointment`` and its bridge modules). The optional features described below each require their own module, indicated in the corresponding section."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:24
msgid "The :guilabel:`Appointments` category of the :ref:`access rights <access-rights/users>` offers:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:26
msgid ":guilabel:`User`: sees and manages their own bookings;"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:27
msgid ":guilabel:`Manager`: sees all bookings, and configures appointment types and resources."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:32
msgid "Appointment types"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:34
msgid "Go to :menuselection:`Appointments --> Configuration --> Appointment Types` to create a type. Fill in the :guilabel:`Name`, a :guilabel:`Description` shown to the customer, the :guilabel:`Location`, and the :guilabel:`Time Zone` the slots are published in."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:39
msgid "Availability"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:41
msgid "The :guilabel:`Availability` tab defines when the type can be booked:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:43
msgid ":guilabel:`Allowed Providers`: the users who can be booked for this type. :guilabel:`Default Working Hours` sets the working schedule used to compute the slots, and, under :guilabel:`Per-provider Working Hours`, a different schedule can be set for individual providers."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:46
msgid ":guilabel:`Required Resources`: resources (rooms, equipment) that must be free for the booking to be possible."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:48
msgid ":guilabel:`Weekly Slots`: the recurring time ranges of the week when bookings are accepted, with an optional capacity or gap override per slot."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:50
msgid ":guilabel:`Duration`: the :guilabel:`Min Duration (min)`, :guilabel:`Max Duration (min)`, :guilabel:`Duration Step (min)`, and :guilabel:`Default Duration (min)` a customer can choose from, and the :guilabel:`Slot Increment (min)` used to generate the proposed start times."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:53
msgid ":guilabel:`Buffers & Gaps`: :guilabel:`Buffer Before (min)` and :guilabel:`Buffer After (min)` keep time free around a booking, and :guilabel:`Gap Between Meetings (min)` enforces a pause between two consecutive bookings."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:56
msgid ":guilabel:`Limits`: how far ahead bookings are possible (:guilabel:`Max Days Ahead`), the :guilabel:`Min Notice Hours` before the start, the :guilabel:`Cancel Notice Hours` until which a customer may cancel, the :guilabel:`Max Future Bookings Per Person`, and the :guilabel:`Capacity Per Slot` when several people may book the same slot."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:61
msgid "Odoo computes the free slots from the working hours, the existing bookings, the providers' calendar events, and their :ref:`leaves <appointments/leaves>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:73
msgid "Assignment and approval"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:75
msgid "When several providers are allowed, the :guilabel:`Assign Strategy` decides who gets the booking: :guilabel:`Least Assigned`, :guilabel:`Round Robin`, or :guilabel:`Random`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:78
msgid "Enable :guilabel:`Require Approval` to hold new bookings in the :guilabel:`Requested` state until they are approved. The approval policy is either :guilabel:`Single Approval (Manager)` or :guilabel:`All Providers Must Approve`; in the latter case, each provider gets an approval line on the booking, and can approve or reject it from the booking form or from the link in the approval email."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:84
msgid ":guilabel:`Unconfirmed Expiry (hours)` automatically cancels bookings that are never confirmed."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:87
msgid "Questions"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:89
msgid "The :guilabel:`Form` tab lists the questions asked when booking. Each question has a :guilabel:`Name`, a :guilabel:`Type` (:guilabel:`Short Text`, :guilabel:`Long Text`, :guilabel:`Number`, :guilabel:`Date`, :guilabel:`Select`, :guilabel:`Checkbox`, or :guilabel:`File`), and can be marked :guilabel:`Required`. For a :guilabel:`Select` question, list the options one per line. A question can also block the booking when a given answer is given, with the :guilabel:`Error Message` shown to the customer."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:96
msgid "The answers are stored on the booking, in its :guilabel:`Answers` tab."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:99
msgid "Notifications"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:101
msgid "In the :guilabel:`Notifications` tab, select the email template used for each step: :guilabel:`Email on Request`, :guilabel:`Email on Confirm`, :guilabel:`Email on Reject`, :guilabel:`Email on Cancel`, :guilabel:`Email on Approval Request`, and :guilabel:`Email on Waitlist Offer`. An :guilabel:`Additional email message` is appended to these emails."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:106
msgid ":guilabel:`Event reminders` send a reminder to the requester a given time before the appointment (e.g., `1` :guilabel:`Days`), while :guilabel:`Calendar alarms` are the reminders set on the provider's calendar event."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:111
msgid "Waitlist"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:113
msgid "Enable :guilabel:`Waitlist` in the corresponding tab to let customers queue for a fully booked slot. When a slot frees up, Odoo offers it to the first customers in the queue (:guilabel:`Waitlist Notify Batch`), who then have :guilabel:`Waitlist Hold Minutes` to confirm before the offer expires and the next customers are notified."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:119
msgid "Visibility and restrictions"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:121
msgid ":guilabel:`Visibility`: :guilabel:`Public`, :guilabel:`Unlisted` (only reachable with the link), or :guilabel:`Private`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:123
msgid "In the :guilabel:`Restrictions` tab, :guilabel:`Allowed Domains` limits public booking to a comma-separated list of email domains."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:125
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Generate share link` to obtain a :guilabel:`Share URL` that can be sent to customers. :guilabel:`Regenerate` invalidates the previous link."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:129
msgid "Pricing and payment"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:131
msgid "A type can be free, or priced with a :guilabel:`Pricing Mode`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:133
msgid ":guilabel:`Fixed`: the :guilabel:`Fixed Amount` is charged per booking;"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:134
msgid ":guilabel:`Hourly`: the :guilabel:`Hourly Rate` is applied to the booked duration, rounded up to the :guilabel:`Billing Increment (min)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:137
msgid "Enable :guilabel:`Payment Required` to make the payment part of the booking flow. :guilabel:`Allow Refund Until Hours` defines until when a cancellation is refundable."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:143
msgid "Bookings"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:145
msgid ":menuselection:`Appointments --> Bookings` lists all bookings, in list or calendar view. A booking records:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:148
msgid "the :guilabel:`Appointment Type`, the :guilabel:`Providers`, and the :guilabel:`Resources`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:149
msgid "the :guilabel:`Customer`, or, for a public booking, the visitor's name, email, phone, and language;"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:151
msgid "the start, the end, and the :guilabel:`Duration (min)`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:152
msgid "the :guilabel:`Status`: :guilabel:`Requested`, :guilabel:`Approved`, :guilabel:`Rejected`, or :guilabel:`Cancelled`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:154
msgid "the :guilabel:`Pricing` and the payment status (:guilabel:`Pending`, :guilabel:`Authorized`, :guilabel:`Paid`, :guilabel:`Refunded`, or :guilabel:`Failed`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:157
msgid "Use the buttons in the header to :guilabel:`Approve`, :guilabel:`Reject`, or :guilabel:`Cancel` a booking, and, after the appointment, to :guilabel:`Mark Show` or :guilabel:`Mark No-show`. :guilabel:`Force Approve` lets a manager approve a booking that is still waiting for other providers."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:162
msgid "An approved booking creates the calendar event of its providers, and the customer receives the confirmation email with a link to their booking."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:176
msgid "Export bookings"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:178
msgid "With the *eYssen Appointment (Reports & Export)* module (`appointment_reports`), appointment managers can download the bookings from the :guilabel:`Export` menu of the application:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:181
msgid ":menuselection:`Appointments --> Export --> Export Bookings (CSV, max 10,000)` downloads the `appointments.csv` file, with one row per booking: name, type, start, end, duration in minutes, customer (or the visitor's name for a public booking), amount, status, and attendance;"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:184
msgid ":menuselection:`Appointments --> Export --> Export Bookings (iCal, max 10,000)` downloads the `appointments.ics` calendar file, which can be imported in any calendar application. Each booking is an event titled with the appointment type and the booking name, with its location and description; approved bookings are marked as confirmed, the others as tentative."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:189
msgid "Both files contain the 10,000 most recent bookings at most, of all statuses. The dates and times are expressed in UTC."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:193
msgid "The export can be narrowed by adding parameters to the address of the download, e.g., `/appointment/export/csv?state=approved&date_from=2026-01-01&date_to=2026-03-31`. The available parameters are `type_id` (the ID of an appointment type), `state` (`requested`, `approved`, `rejected`, or `cancelled`), `date_from`, and `date_to` (`YYYY-MM-DD`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:199
msgid "To install the module, enable :guilabel:`Reports` under :guilabel:`Appointment` in :menuselection:`Settings --> eYssen ERP`. The menu and the downloads are reserved for the users with the :guilabel:`Manager` access level of the Appointments app."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:206
msgid "Provider unavailability"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:208
msgid "Providers can be made unavailable for a period of time with an **appointment leave**, which has a :guilabel:`User`, a start and an end, a :guilabel:`Reason`, and a state (:guilabel:`Draft`, :guilabel:`Approved`, :guilabel:`Cancelled`). Only approved leaves block the slots."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:213
msgid "With the *Appointment (HR Holidays)* (``appointment_hr``) module, validated time off of the employees linked to the providers also blocks the corresponding slots, so time off does not have to be entered twice."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:218
msgid "Passes"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:220
msgid "The *Appointment (Passes)* (``appointment_pass``) module sells packages of appointments. In :menuselection:`Appointments --> Passes --> Pass Products`, define a pass with a :guilabel:`Name`, a :guilabel:`Mode` (a number of :guilabel:`Occurrences` or a balance of minutes), the :guilabel:`Validity (days)`, and the :guilabel:`Price`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:225
msgid ":menuselection:`Appointments --> Passes --> Pass Holders` lists the passes owned by customers, with their :guilabel:`Occurrences Remaining` or :guilabel:`Minutes Remaining` and the :guilabel:`Valid Until` date. When a customer with a valid pass books an appointment, the booking is redeemed against the pass instead of being paid."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:231
msgid "Coupons and gift cards"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:233
msgid "The *Appointment (Payment)* (``appointment_payment``) module adds discounts to the booking flow:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:235
msgid ":menuselection:`Appointments --> Configuration --> Payments & Discounts --> Coupons`: a coupon has a :guilabel:`Code`, a :guilabel:`Discount Type` (percentage or fixed amount), an :guilabel:`Amount`, a validity period, and a :guilabel:`Max Uses` limit (`0` = unlimited)."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:238
msgid ":menuselection:`Appointments --> Configuration --> Payments & Discounts --> Gift Cards`: a gift card has a :guilabel:`Code`, a :guilabel:`Balance`, and an expiry date. The balance is deducted from the amount due of the booking."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:242
msgid "The remaining :guilabel:`Amount Due` is then paid with one of the configured :doc:`payment providers <../finance/payment_providers>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:246
msgid "Other integrations"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:248
msgid "**Project**: with the *Appointment (Project Tasks)* (``appointment_project``) module, select a :guilabel:`Target Project` on the appointment type to create a task there when a booking is approved."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:251
msgid "**eLearning**: with the *Appointment (eLearning)* (``appointment_elearning``) module, select a :guilabel:`Course to Enroll` on the appointment type to enroll the customer in that course when the booking is approved."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments.rst:254
msgid "**CRM**: see :doc:`appointments/create-opps`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments/create-opps.rst:3
msgid "Create leads from bookings"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments/create-opps.rst:5
msgid "With the *Appointment (CRM)* (``appointment_crm``) module, an approved booking can automatically create a lead or an opportunity in the :doc:`CRM <../../sales/crm>` pipeline, so that the sales team follows up on the customers who booked a meeting."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments/create-opps.rst:12
msgid "Go to :menuselection:`Appointments --> Configuration --> Appointment Types`, open the relevant type, and enable :guilabel:`Create CRM Lead`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments/create-opps.rst:15
msgid "In :guilabel:`Lead Title`, define the title of the lead created. Use `{customer}` as a placeholder for the customer name, e.g. `New appointment: {customer}`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments/create-opps.rst:27
msgid "Use the leads"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments/create-opps.rst:29
msgid "When a booking of that type is approved, Odoo creates the lead with the customer's contact details and the answers given while booking, and links it to the booking in the :guilabel:`Related Lead` field. Opening the field brings the salesperson directly to the pipeline record."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/appointments/create-opps.rst:34
msgid "Leads are created on approval, so bookings that stay :guilabel:`Requested`, or that are rejected, do not generate a lead."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:7
msgid "Odoo **Calendar** is a scheduling app that allows users to integrate a company's business flow into a single management platform. By integrating with the other apps in Odoo's ecosystem, **Calendar** allows users to schedule and organize meetings, schedule events, plan performance reviews, coordinate projects, and more – all from the same platform."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:12
msgid "Upon opening the :menuselection:`Calendar app`, users have an overview of their current meetings. The selected view option appears as a :guilabel:`Day`, :guilabel:`Week`, :guilabel:`Month`, or :guilabel:`Year` drop-down menu. Under the view options drop-down menu, users can also enable or disable :guilabel:`Show weekends`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:25
msgid "Depending on the selected view option, users can click the :icon:`oi-arrow-left` :icon:`oi-arrow-right` :guilabel:`(left or right arrow)` buttons to switch between days, weeks, etc., and switch back to the current day with the :guilabel:`Today` button."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:30
msgid "Sync third-party calendars"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:32
msgid "Users can sync Odoo with existing :doc:`Outlook <calendar/outlook>` and/or :doc:`Google <calendar/google>` calendars, by heading to :menuselection:`Calendar app --> Configuration --> Settings`. From here, enter :guilabel:`Client ID` and :guilabel:`Client Secret`. There is also an option to pause synchronization by ticking the checkbox, or automating synchronization by keeping it blank."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:38
msgid "Once the desired configurations are complete, be sure to click :guilabel:`Save` before moving on."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:40
msgid "Events created in synced calendars automatically appear across the integrated platforms."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:43
msgid ":doc:`Synchronize Outlook calendar with Odoo <calendar/outlook>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:44
msgid ":doc:`Synchronize Google calendar with Odoo <calendar/google>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:47
msgid "Create activities from chatter"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:49
msgid "Instantly create new meetings anywhere in Odoo through an individual record's chatter, like in a **CRM** opportunity card or task in the **Projects** app."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:52
msgid "From the chatter, click on the :guilabel:`Activities` button. In the :guilabel:`Schedule Activity` pop-up window, select the desired :guilabel:`Activity Type`, which populates a set of buttons, depending on the activity."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:56
msgid "Activities that involve other schedules, like :guilabel:`Meeting` or :guilabel:`Call for Demo`, link to the **Calendar** app. Select one of these activities to link to the **Calendar** app, then hit :guilabel:`Open Calendar` to navigate back to the app. Alternatively, it is also possible to :guilabel:`Schedule & Mark as Done` to close out the activity, or select :guilabel:`Done & Schedule Next` to keep the :guilabel:`Schedule Activity` window open to create another."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:63
msgid ":doc:`Schedule activities in Odoo <../essentials/activities>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:66
msgid "Plan an event"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:68
msgid "To put an event on the calendar, open the :menuselection:`Calendar app`, and click into the target date. On the :guilabel:`New Event` pop-up window that appears, start by adding the event title."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:79
msgid "The target date auto-populates in the :guilabel:`Start` field. This can be changed by clicking into the date section, and selecting a date from the calendar. For multi-day events, select the end date in the second field, then click :guilabel:`Apply`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:83
msgid "Tick the :guilabel:`All Day` checkbox if there is no specific start or end time."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:85
msgid "For events with specific start and stop times, ensure the :guilabel:`All Day` checkbox is unticked to enable time selection. With the :guilabel:`All Day` checkbox unticked, time selections appear in the :guilabel:`Start` field."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:89
msgid "The signed-in user auto-populates as the first attendee. Additional :guilabel:`Attendees` can be added or created from here, as well."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:92
msgid "For virtual meetings, copy and paste the URL into the space provided in the :guilabel:`Videocall URL` field. Or, click :icon:`fa-plus` :guilabel:`Odoo meeting` to create a link."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:96
msgid "Next, either create the event by clicking :guilabel:`Save & Close`, or select :guilabel:`More Options` to further configure the event."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:100
msgid "Once the event is created, users can click into the virtual meeting directly from the calendar event to access more configuration options."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:110
msgid "The :guilabel:`Description` field allows users to add additional information and details about the meeting."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:113
msgid "Click :guilabel:`More Options` to navigate to the meeting form, which provides additional configurations for the event:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:116
msgid ":guilabel:`Duration`: Define the length of the meeting in :guilabel:`hours`, or toggle the :guilabel:`All Day` switch."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:118
msgid ":guilabel:`Recurrent`: Tick the checkbox to create a recurring meeting. Once selected, this opens new fields:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:121
msgid ":guilabel:`Timezone`: Select the timezone for which this meeting time is specified."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:122
msgid ":guilabel:`Repeat`: Select the recurring period of this meeting. Depending on what type of recurrence has been selected, a subsequent field appears, in which users can indicate when the meeting should recur. For example, if :guilabel:`Monthly` is selected as the :guilabel:`Repeat` option, a new field appears, in which the user decides on what :guilabel:`Day of Month` the meeting should recur."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:127
msgid ":guilabel:`Until`: Select the limited :guilabel:`Number of repetitions` this meeting should recur, the :guilabel:`End date` of when the recurrences should stop, or if the meetings should recur :guilabel:`Forever`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:130
msgid ":guilabel:`Tags`: Add tags to the event, like `Customer Meeting` or `Internal Meeting`. These can be searched and filtered in the **Calendar** app when organizing multiple events."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:132
msgid ":guilabel:`Appointment`: Link existing or new appointments. These can be configured through the :ref:`Share Availabilities <calendar/share-availabilities>` button from the main **Calendar** dashboard."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:135
msgid ":guilabel:`Privacy`: Toggle between visibility options to control who can view the event."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:136
msgid ":guilabel:`Organizer`: This is defaulted to the current Odoo user. Select a new one from existing users, or create and edit a new user."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:138
msgid ":guilabel:`Description`: Add additional information or details about the meeting."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:139
msgid ":guilabel:`Reminders`: Select notification options to send to attendees. Choose a default notification, or configure new reminders."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:143
msgid "Coordinate with teams' availability"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:145
msgid "When scheduling an event for multiple users, on the **Calendar** app dashboard, tick the checkbox next to :guilabel:`Attendees` to view team members' availability. Tick (or untick) the checkbox next to listed users to show (or hide) individual calendars."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:160
msgid "Share availabilities"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:162
msgid "To let customers or colleagues book a slot in your calendar themselves, use the :doc:`Appointments app <appointments>`: it publishes the bookable slots, applies the booking rules, and creates the calendar event of the provider once a booking is approved."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/calendar.rst:167
msgid "Automatic video call"
