#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards.rst:165
msgid "Access rights and sharing"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards.rst:170
msgid "Consulting dashboards"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards.rst:172
msgid "The *right to view and interact with a dashboard* is based on :ref:`user groups <access-rights/groups>`, and is managed in the :ref:`Configuration settings <dashboards/configuration>` of the Dashboards app. Only users who are part of a group that has been granted access to a specific dashboard see that dashboard in the left-hand panel on the main Dashboards page."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards.rst:178
msgid "However, the *visibility of dynamic data within a dashboard* is handled separately. This is based on a user's :ref:`access rights <access-rights/users>` to the model from which the data has been retrieved, and takes into account any record rules that may restrict access."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards.rst:183
msgid "User permissions are taken into account when a user opens a dashboard, with the dashboard only being populated with data the user is authorized to see. This means that a user could in theory be able to view a dashboard but, due to a lack of appropriate permissions, not be able to see the data the dashboard's creator intended to be displayed."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards.rst:188
msgid "Therefore, it is crucial to take user permissions into consideration when granting dashboard access to groups."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards.rst:192
msgid "Granting the user group `Sales / User: Own Documents Only` access to the :guilabel:`Sales` dashboard would serve little purpose. While users belonging to that group would be able to view and interact with the dashboard, they would only see data related to their own sales, rendering the overall dashboard misleading."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards.rst:197
msgid "To manage users' rights to view and interact with a dashboard:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards.rst:199
msgid "In the Dashboards app, go to :menuselection:`Configuration --> Dashboards`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards.rst:200
msgid "From the list of dashboard sections, open the relevant section."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards.rst:201
msgid "On the line of the relevant dashboard, in the :guilabel:`Group` column:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards.rst:203
msgid "add a user group by clicking the field until a dropdown with user groups appears, then selecting the appropriate user group. In the dropdown, click :guilabel:`Search More` to access the full list of user groups;"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards.rst:206
msgid "remove a user group by clicking the relevant group name, then clicking :icon:`fa-times` :guilabel:`(Delete)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards.rst:212
msgid "Share dashboard snapshot"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards.rst:214
msgid "To share a frozen version of a dashboard with an internal user who does not have the appropriate access, or with an external party, click :icon:`fa-share-alt` :guilabel:`Share` at the top-right of the page, then click the :icon:`fa-clone` :guilabel:`(copy)` icon to copy a shareable link to the clipboard. Anyone with the link can open the read-only snapshot without logging in."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards/custom_dashboards.rst:3
msgid "Custom dashboards"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards/custom_dashboards.rst:5
msgid "The *Dashboard* module (``dashboard``) adds a second, fully configurable dashboard application. Unlike the standard dashboards, custom dashboards are built record by record: each dashboard (or *board*) is a grid of *widgets* — charts, |KPIs|, tables, and shortcuts — that read live data from the database."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards/custom_dashboards.rst:14
msgid "This documentation describes the *Dashboard* (``dashboard``) module. The standard, pre-configured dashboards described in :doc:`../dashboards` are provided by a different application, which also uses the name :guilabel:`Dashboards`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards/custom_dashboards.rst:21
msgid "The module defines three access levels in the :guilabel:`Dashboard` category of a user's :ref:`access rights <access-rights/users>`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards/custom_dashboards.rst:24
msgid ":guilabel:`User`: can open the dashboards they have been granted access to."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards/custom_dashboards.rst:25
msgid ":guilabel:`Manager`: can create and configure dashboards and widgets, and manage the layout."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards/custom_dashboards.rst:26
msgid ":guilabel:`Technical (Python / SQL)`: can additionally create widgets whose data comes from Python code or an SQL query."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards/custom_dashboards.rst:30
msgid "Python and SQL widgets run with full database access, bypassing access rights and record rules. Grant the :guilabel:`Technical (Python / SQL)` level only to users who are trusted with reading the entire database."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards/custom_dashboards.rst:35
msgid "Create a dashboard"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards/custom_dashboards.rst:37
msgid "To create a dashboard, go to :menuselection:`Dashboards --> Configuration --> Boards` and click :guilabel:`New`. Fill in:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards/custom_dashboards.rst:40
msgid ":guilabel:`Dashboard Name`: the name shown in the menu and at the top of the dashboard."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards/custom_dashboards.rst:41
msgid ":guilabel:`Menu Sequence`: the position of the dashboard's menu item."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards/custom_dashboards.rst:42
msgid ":guilabel:`Also show under`: optionally, another app's menu (e.g., :guilabel:`Sales`) where a menu item for this dashboard is created as well, in addition to the entry in the Dashboards app."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards/custom_dashboards.rst:44
msgid ":guilabel:`Auto Refresh`: how often the dashboard reloads its data — :guilabel:`Off`, :guilabel:`15 seconds`, :guilabel:`30 seconds`, :guilabel:`1 minute`, or :guilabel:`5 minutes`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards/custom_dashboards.rst:46
msgid ":guilabel:`Allowed Groups` and :guilabel:`Allowed Users`: who may open the dashboard. If both are empty, every user with :guilabel:`Dashboard / User` rights sees it."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards/custom_dashboards.rst:49
msgid "The :guilabel:`System` section shows the client action and the menu items Odoo created for the dashboard; these fields are read-only."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards/custom_dashboards.rst:52
msgid "Click :guilabel:`View Dashboard` in the header to open the dashboard itself."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards/custom_dashboards.rst:63
msgid "Arrange the layout"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards/custom_dashboards.rst:65
msgid "On the dashboard itself, widgets are placed on a grid. Managers can drag a widget by its header to move it and drag its bottom-right corner to resize it. The layout is stored per dashboard, so all users see the same arrangement."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards/custom_dashboards.rst:77
msgid "Widgets"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards/custom_dashboards.rst:79
msgid "Widgets are managed from the :guilabel:`Widgets` tab of a dashboard, or from :menuselection:`Dashboards --> Configuration --> Widgets`. Each widget has a :guilabel:`Name`, a :guilabel:`Type`, and — except for shortcuts — a :guilabel:`Data Source`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards/custom_dashboards.rst:84
msgid "Data source"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards/custom_dashboards.rst:86
msgid ":guilabel:`ORM`: the widget reads a model through the standard database layer, so the user's access rights and record rules apply. Select the :guilabel:`Model`, the :guilabel:`Category / Group By` field and, for hierarchical charts, a :guilabel:`Sub / Secondary Group By` field. A :guilabel:`Domain Filter`, a :guilabel:`Date Filter Field` with a :guilabel:`Date Range`, a :guilabel:`Limit`, and the sorting (:guilabel:`Sort By`, :guilabel:`Sort Order`) further restrict the data. For records linked through a many2many or one2many field, :guilabel:`M2M / O2M Aggregation` decides whether a record is counted once for each related record or only once, and :guilabel:`Include Empty Category` adds a bucket for records with no value."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards/custom_dashboards.rst:94
msgid ":guilabel:`Python`: the widget is filled by a short Python snippet that populates a result dictionary."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards/custom_dashboards.rst:96
msgid ":guilabel:`SQL`: the widget is filled by a `SELECT` query. The first column provides the labels, the remaining columns the values. Statements that modify data are rejected."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards/custom_dashboards.rst:99
msgid "Both :guilabel:`Python` and :guilabel:`SQL` are edited in the :guilabel:`Custom Code` tab and are only available to users with the :guilabel:`Technical (Python / SQL)` access level."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards/custom_dashboards.rst:103
msgid "Measures"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards/custom_dashboards.rst:105
msgid "In the :guilabel:`Measures` list, add the fields to plot or aggregate. For each measure, select the :guilabel:`Field`, the :guilabel:`Aggregation`, an optional :guilabel:`Label` and :guilabel:`Color`, and — for dual-axis charts — the :guilabel:`Y Axis` to use."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards/custom_dashboards.rst:110
msgid "Charts"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards/custom_dashboards.rst:112
msgid "Set the :guilabel:`Chart Type` to :guilabel:`Bar`, :guilabel:`Line`, :guilabel:`Area`, :guilabel:`Pie`, :guilabel:`Radar`, :guilabel:`Funnel`, :guilabel:`Gauge`, :guilabel:`Scatter`, :guilabel:`Heatmap`, :guilabel:`Treemap`, :guilabel:`Sunburst`, :guilabel:`Dual Sunburst`, :guilabel:`Sankey`, :guilabel:`Stacked Bar (Hierarchical)`, or :guilabel:`Bubble / Scatter`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards/custom_dashboards.rst:117
msgid "Depending on the chart type, further options appear: :guilabel:`Orientation` and :guilabel:`Stacking` for bars, :guilabel:`Smooth`, :guilabel:`Show Dots` and :guilabel:`Step` for lines, :guilabel:`Doughnut Style`, :guilabel:`Top N (0=all)`, :guilabel:`Group Others` and :guilabel:`Label Format` for pies, or :guilabel:`Min` and :guilabel:`Max` for gauges. :guilabel:`Show Legend` and :guilabel:`Show Labels` control the chart decorations, and :guilabel:`Theme` switches between the :guilabel:`Default`, :guilabel:`Dark`, and :guilabel:`Vintage` color themes."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards/custom_dashboards.rst:126
msgid "Hierarchical chart types (treemap, sunburst, dual sunburst, sankey, hierarchical stacked bar, bubble) display two levels of data and therefore require a :guilabel:`Sub / Secondary Group By` field."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards/custom_dashboards.rst:139
msgid "|KPIs|"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards/custom_dashboards.rst:141
msgid "A |KPI| widget shows a single aggregated figure. Set an :guilabel:`Icon`, an optional :guilabel:`Target` value, and a :guilabel:`Compare Period` to display the variation against the previous period."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/dashboards/custom_dashboards.rst:146
msgid "Tables"
msgstr ""

