#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/data_cleaning.rst:3
msgid "Data Cleaning"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/data_cleaning.rst:5
msgid "The **Data Cleaning** app keeps the database free of old and outdated records: customizable rules detect the records that have not changed for a given period of time, and either archive or delete them."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/data_cleaning.rst:10
msgid "The app is provided by the *Data Recycle* (``data_recycle``) module."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/data_cleaning.rst:15
msgid "Recycle records"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/data_cleaning.rst:17
msgid "The :guilabel:`Recycle Records` dashboard displays the records detected by the :ref:`recycle rules <data_cleaning/recylce-rule>`. Go to :menuselection:`Data Cleaning --> Recycle Records`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/data_cleaning.rst:20
msgid "The :guilabel:`RECYCLE RULES` sidebar lists each of the active recycle rules. By default, the :guilabel:`All` option is selected, and the records are displayed with the following columns:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/data_cleaning.rst:23
msgid ":guilabel:`Record ID`: the ID of the original record;"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/data_cleaning.rst:24
msgid ":guilabel:`Record Name`: the name or title of the original record."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/data_cleaning.rst:26
msgid "Select a specific rule in the :guilabel:`RECYCLE RULES` sidebar to filter the records."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/data_cleaning.rst:28
msgid "To recycle a record, click the :icon:`fa-check` :guilabel:`Validate` button on its row. Depending on how the rule is configured, the record is then archived or deleted from the database."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/data_cleaning.rst:32
msgid "Discard a proposal by clicking the :icon:`fa-times` :guilabel:`Discard` button. The record is hidden from the list, and is not detected by the recycle rule again in the future."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/data_cleaning.rst:35
msgid "View discarded records by selecting the :guilabel:`Discarded` filter from the :ref:`search bar <search/filters>` drop-down menu."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/data_cleaning.rst:48
msgid "Recycle record rules"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/data_cleaning.rst:50
msgid "The *recycle rules* set the conditions for how records are recycled. They can be configured for each model in the database, and with varying levels of specificity. To get started, go to :menuselection:`Data Cleaning --> Configuration --> Rules --> Recycle Records`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/data_cleaning.rst:55
msgid "Recycle rules run once a day, as part of the *Data Recycle: Clean Records* scheduled action. However, each rule can be :ref:`run manually <data-cleaning/run-recycle-rule>` at any time."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/data_cleaning.rst:58
msgid "By default, no recycle rules exist. Click :guilabel:`New` to create one."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/data_cleaning.rst:60
msgid "On the rule form, first choose a :guilabel:`Model` for the rule to target. Selecting a model updates the rule title to the chosen model."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/data_cleaning.rst:63
msgid "Optionally, configure a :guilabel:`Filter` to specify the records eligible for this rule. The number of eligible records is shown in the :icon:`oi-arrow-right` :guilabel:`# record(s)` link."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/data_cleaning.rst:66
msgid "Next, configure the field and time range the rule uses to detect the records to recycle:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/data_cleaning.rst:68
msgid ":guilabel:`Time Field`: select a date or datetime field of the model to base the time on;"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/data_cleaning.rst:69
msgid ":guilabel:`Delta`: type the length of time, which must be a whole number (e.g. `7`);"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/data_cleaning.rst:70
msgid ":guilabel:`Delta Unit`: select the unit of time (:guilabel:`Days`, :guilabel:`Weeks`, :guilabel:`Months`, or :guilabel:`Years`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/data_cleaning.rst:73
msgid "Then, select a :guilabel:`Recycle Mode`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/data_cleaning.rst:75
msgid ":guilabel:`Manual`: each detected record must be validated manually on the :ref:`Recycle Records dashboard <data_cleaning/recycle>`. This mode enables the :guilabel:`Notify Users` field, where the administrators to inform can be selected, together with the notification frequency (:guilabel:`Notify` every *n* :guilabel:`Days`, :guilabel:`Weeks`, or :guilabel:`Months`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/data_cleaning.rst:79
msgid ":guilabel:`Automatic`: the detected records are recycled automatically, without notifying users."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/data_cleaning.rst:81
msgid "Lastly, select a :guilabel:`Recycle Action` to either :guilabel:`Archive` or :guilabel:`Delete` the records. If :guilabel:`Delete` is selected, choose whether or not to :guilabel:`Include Archived` records in the rule."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/data_cleaning.rst:86
msgid "The :guilabel:`Archive` action is only available for models that have an :guilabel:`Active` field; otherwise, Odoo raises an error when the rule is saved."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/data_cleaning.rst:89
msgid "With the rule's configuration complete, either close the rule form, or :ref:`run the rule manually <data-cleaning/run-recycle-rule>` to instantly capture records to recycle."
