#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/canned_responses.rst:3
msgid "Canned responses"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/canned_responses.rst:5
msgid "*Canned responses* are customizable inputs where a typed shortcut populates a longer response. A user enters a keyword shortcut, which is then automatically replaced by the expanded substitution response. Canned responses save time by allowing users to use shorthand phrases to populate longer messages. This also limits the possibility of errors when typing out longer messages because these are pre-set messages. This maintains consistency throughout customer interactions."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/canned_responses.rst:11
msgid "Canned responses consist of two main components: the *shortcut* and the *substitution*. The shortcut is the keyword or key phrase that is to be replaced. The substitution is the longer message that replaces the shortcut."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/canned_responses.rst:22
msgid "Canned responses are available :ref:`to use <discuss/use-cases>` in **Live Chat** conversations, the **Discuss** app, and the *Chatter* composer. This includes direct message conversations, channel conversations, and **WhatsApp** messages."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/canned_responses.rst:29
msgid "Creating canned responses"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/canned_responses.rst:31
msgid "Canned responses are managed through the **Discuss** application. To create a new canned response, or manage the list of existing responses, navigate to :menuselection:`Discuss app --> Configuration --> Canned Responses`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/canned_responses.rst:35
msgid "Then, to create a new canned response, click :guilabel:`New` at the top-left of the list. Doing so reveals a new blank line in the list."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/canned_responses.rst:38
msgid "Canned responses consist of two main components, a *shortcut* the user enters, and the *substitution* that replaces the shortcut."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/canned_responses.rst:49
msgid "Type a shortcut command in the :guilabel:`Shortcut` field. Next, click on the :guilabel:`Substitution` field, and type the message that will replace the shortcut."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/canned_responses.rst:53
msgid "Try to connect the shortcut to the topic of the substitution. Not only does this make it easier to use the responses, it prevents the list of responses from becoming disorganized and overwhelming."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/canned_responses.rst:57
msgid "In the :guilabel:`Description` field, add any information that provides context for this response, such as guidelines for when it should or should not be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/canned_responses.rst:60
msgid "The :guilabel:`Created by` field automatically populates with the name of the user that creates a new response. This field cannot be edited."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/canned_responses.rst:63
msgid "To :ref:`share <discuss/sharing-responses>` this response with other users, select one or more groups in the :guilabel:`Authorized Group` field that should have access."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/canned_responses.rst:67
msgid "If the :guilabel:`Authorized Group` field is left blank, the response can **only** be used by the user that created it."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/canned_responses.rst:70
msgid "Canned responses created by the database are automatically credited as created by *OdooBot*. They must be assigned to an *authorized group* before they can be used by **any** users. To view the responses created by *OdooBot*, navigate to :menuselection:`Discuss app --> Configuration --> Canned Responses`. Click into the search bar, and remove any filters."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/canned_responses.rst:75
msgid "Lastly, the :guilabel:`Last Used` field keeps track of the date and time each response was most recently used. This field cannot be edited."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/canned_responses.rst:81
msgid "Share responses"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/canned_responses.rst:83
msgid "Canned responses, by default, are made available **only** to the user who creates them. To make a canned response available for others to use, they need to be shared."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/canned_responses.rst:87
msgid "Users with *Administrator* access rights can view and edit canned responses created by other users through the **Discuss** app. However, they are **only** able to use them if they are included in an authorized group that has been designated on that canned responses item line, located on the :guilabel:`Canned Responses` page."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/canned_responses.rst:92
msgid "Access to shared responses is granted on the :ref:`groups <access-rights/groups>` level."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/canned_responses.rst:94
msgid "To view the *Groups* a user is a member of, first enable :ref:`Developer mode <developer-mode>`, then navigate to :menuselection:`Settings app --> Users & Companies --> Users`. Select a user from the list, and click to open their :guilabel:`User Record`. Then, click the :guilabel:`Groups` smart button at the top of the page."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/canned_responses.rst:100
msgid "To view a list of users in a specific group, first enable :doc:`Developer mode <../../general/developer_mode/>`. Next, navigate to :menuselection:`Settings app --> Users & Companies --> Groups`. Select a group from the list, then click to open the :guilabel:`Group Record`. A list of users is included on the :guilabel:`Users` tab."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/canned_responses.rst:105
msgid "After determining what groups should have access to a response, they **must** :ref:`be added <discuss/created-canned-response>` to the :guilabel:`Authorized Groups` field for each canned response."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/canned_responses.rst:110
msgid "The user who created the response can use it, even if they are not a member of one of the *Authorized Groups*."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/canned_responses.rst:116
msgid "Use a canned response"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/canned_responses.rst:118
msgid "Canned responses can be used in the **Discuss** app, in a **Live Chat** conversation, or on any record that contains a *Chatter* composer. This includes direct message conversations, channel conversations, and *WhatsApp* messages."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/canned_responses.rst:122
msgid "To use a canned response, type a colon (`:`) into a *Chatter* composer or chat window, followed by the shortcut. Then press :kbd:`Enter`. This replaces the shortcut with the substitution, though the response can still be edited before it is sent."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/canned_responses.rst:127
msgid "Typing `:` in the *Chatter* composer, or chat window, on its own generates a drop-down list of available canned responses. A response can be selected from the list, in addition to the use of shortcuts."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/canned_responses.rst:131
msgid "To search through the list of available responses, type `:`, followed by the first few letters of the shortcut."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/canned_responses.rst:142
msgid ":doc:`Chatter <chatter>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/canned_responses.rst:143
#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:578
msgid ":doc:`Discuss <../discuss>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/canned_responses.rst:144
msgid ":ref:`Commands and Canned Responses <live-chat/canned-responses>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:3
msgid "Chatter"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:9
msgid "The *Chatter* feature is integrated throughout Odoo to streamline communication, maintain traceability, and provide accountability among team members. Chatter windows, known as *composers*, are located on almost every record within the database, and allow users to communicate with both internal users and external contacts."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:14
msgid "Chatter composers also enable users to log notes, upload files, and schedule activities."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:17
msgid "Chatter thread"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:19
msgid "A *chatter thread* can be found on most pages in the database, and serves as a record of the updates and edits made to a record. A note is logged in the chatter thread when a change is made to the record. The note includes details of the change, and a time stamp."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:24
msgid "A user, Mitchell Admin, needs to update the email address of a contact. After they save the changes to the contact record, a note is logged in the chatter of the contact record with the following information:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:28
msgid "The date when the change occurred."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:29
msgid "The email address as it was previously listed."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:30
msgid "The updated email address."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:39
msgid "If a record was created, or edited, via an imported file, or was otherwise updated through an intervention by the system, the chatter thread creates a log note, and credits the change to OdooBot."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:53
msgid "Add followers"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:55
msgid "A *follower* is a user or contact that is added to a record and is notified when the record is updated, based on specific :ref:`follower subscription settings <discuss/edit-subscription>`. Followers can add themselves, or can be added by another user."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:60
msgid "If a user creates, or is assigned to a record, they are automatically added as a follower."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:62
msgid "To follow a record, navigate to any record with a chatter thread. For example, to open a *CRM* opportunity, navigate to :menuselection:`CRM app --> Sales --> My Pipeline`, and select an opportunity from the list to open it."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:66
msgid "At the top-right, above the chatter composer, click :guilabel:`Follow`. Doing this changes the button to read :guilabel:`Following`. Click it again to :guilabel:`Unfollow`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:70
msgid "Manage followers"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:72
msgid "To add another user, or contact, as a follower, click the |user|. This opens a drop-down list of the current followers. Click :guilabel:`Add Followers` to open an :guilabel:`Invite Follower` pop-up window."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:76
msgid "Select one or more contacts from the :guilabel:`Recipients` drop-down list. To notify the contacts, tick the :guilabel:`Send Notification` checkbox. Edit the message template as desired, then click :guilabel:`Add Followers`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:80
msgid "To remove followers, click the |user| to open the current followers list. Find the name of the follower to be removed, and click the :icon:`fa-remove` :guilabel:`(remove)` icon."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:86
msgid "Edit follower subscription"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:88
msgid "The updates a follower receives can vary based on their subscription settings. To see the type of updates a follower is subscribed to, and to edit the list, click the |user|. Find the appropriate follower in the list, then click the :icon:`fa-pencil` :guilabel:`(pencil)` icon. This opens the :guilabel:`Edit Subscription` pop-up window for the follower."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:93
msgid "The list of available subscription settings varies depending on the record type. For example, a follower of a *Project* task may be informed when the task's stage changes. This option would not be available for the followers of a *CRM* opportunity."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:97
msgid "Tick the checkbox for any updates the follower should receive, and clear the checkbox for any updates they should **not** receive. Click :guilabel:`Apply` when finished."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:111
msgid "Log notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:113
msgid "The chatter function includes the ability to log internal notes on individual records. These notes are only accessible to internal users, and are available on any records that feature a chatter thread."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:117
msgid "To log an internal note, first navigate to a record. For example, to open a *CRM* opportunity, navigate to :menuselection:`CRM app --> Sales --> My Pipeline`, and click on the Kanban card of an opportunity to open it. Then, at the top-right, above the chatter composer, click :guilabel:`Log note`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:122
msgid "Enter the note in the chatter composer. To tag an internal user, type `@`, and begin typing the name of the person to tag. Then, select a name from the drop-down menu. Depending on their notification settings, the user is notified by email, or through Odoo."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:127
msgid "Outside contacts can also be tagged in an internal log note. The contact then receives an email with the contents of the note they were tagged in, including any attachments added directly to the note. If they respond to the email, their response is logged in the chatter, and they are added to the record as a follower."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:132
msgid "Outside contacts are **not** able to log in to view the entire chatter thread, and are only notified of specific updates, based on their :ref:`follower subscription settings <discuss/edit-subscription>`, or when they are tagged directly."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:139
msgid "Send messages"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:141
msgid "Chatter composers can send messages to outside contacts, without having to leave the database, or open a different application. This makes it easy to communicate with potential customers in the *Sales* and *CRM* applications, or vendors in the *Purchase* app."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:145
msgid "To send a message, first navigate to a record. For example, to send a message from a *CRM* opportunity, navigate to :menuselection:`CRM app --> Sales --> My Pipeline`, and click on the Kanban card of an opportunity to open it. Then, at the top-right, above the chatter composer, click :guilabel:`Send message`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:151
msgid "Press :command:`Ctrl + Enter` to send a message, instead of using the :guilabel:`Send` button."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:153
msgid "If any :ref:`followers <discuss/add-followers>` have been added to the record, they are added as recipients of the message."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:157
msgid ":ref:`Followers <discuss/add-followers>` of a record are added as recipients of a message automatically. If a follower should **not** receive a message, they must be removed as a follower before the message is sent, or a note is logged."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:170
msgid "Expand full composer"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:172
msgid "The chatter composer can be expanded to a larger pop-up window, allowing for additional customizations."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:175
msgid "To open the full composer, click the :icon:`fa-expand` :guilabel:`(expand)` icon in the bottom-right corner of the composer window."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:185
msgid "Doing this opens a :guilabel:`Compose Email` pop-up window. Confirm or edit the intended :guilabel:`Recipients` of the message, or add additional recipients. The :guilabel:`Subject` field auto-populates based on the title of the record, though it can be edited, if desired."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:189
msgid "To use an :doc:`email template <../../general/companies/email_template/>` for the message, click the |ve| icon, then select a template from the list. Existing templates can also be overwritten or deleted from this menu."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:194
msgid "The number and type of templates available vary, based on the record the message is created from."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:196
msgid "Click :icon:`fa-paperclip` :guilabel:`(paperclip)` icon to add any files to the message, then click :guilabel:`Send`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:207
msgid "Generate text with AI"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:209
msgid "To generate message text using AI, click the AI icon from the expanded chatter composer. This opens a :guilabel:`Generate Text with AI` pop-up."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:212
msgid "Enter a prompt in the :guilabel:`Send a message` field to instruct the AI on the type of content needed, then press enter, or click the :icon:`fa-paper-plane` :guilabel:`(paper plane)` icon."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:222
msgid "After the text is generated, click :guilabel:`Insert` to insert the text into the message composer."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:225
msgid "Before sending the final message, be sure to edit any commentary from the AI, or any text in brackets."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:235
msgid "Edit sent messages"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:237
msgid "Messages can be edited after they are sent, to fix typos, correct mistakes, or add missing information."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:241
msgid "When messages are edited after they have been sent, an updated message is **not** sent to the recipient."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:244
msgid "To edit a sent message, click the |ve| menu to the right of the message. Then, select :guilabel:`Edit`. Make any necessary adjustments to the message."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:254
msgid "To save the changes, press :command:`Ctrl + Enter`. To discard the changes, press :command:`Escape`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:257
msgid "Users with Admin-level access rights can edit any sent messages. Users without Admin rights can **only** edit messages they created."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:263
msgid "Search messages"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:265
msgid "Chatter threads can become long after a while, because of all the information they contain. To make it easier to find a specific entry, users can search the text of messages and notes for specific keywords."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:269
msgid "First, select a record with a chatter thread. For example, to search a *CRM* opportunity, navigate to :menuselection:`CRM app --> Sales --> My Pipeline`, and click on the Kanban card of an opportunity to open it. Then, at the top-right, above the chatter composer, click the :icon:`oi-search` :guilabel:`(search)` icon to open the search bar."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:274
msgid "Enter a keyword or phrase into the search bar, then hit :command:`Enter`, or click the :icon:`oi-search` :guilabel:`(search)` icon to the right of the search bar. Any messages or notes containing the keyword or phrase entered are listed below the search bar, with the keyword highlighted."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:279
msgid "To be taken directly to a particular message in the chatter thread, hover over the upper-right corner of the result to reveal a :guilabel:`Jump` button. Click this button to be directed to that message's location in the thread."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:293
msgid "Schedule activities"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:295
msgid "*Activities* are follow-up tasks tied to a record in an Odoo database. Activities can be scheduled on any database page that contains a chatter thread, Kanban view, list view, or activities view of an application."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:299
msgid "To schedule an activity through a chatter thread, click the :guilabel:`Activities` button, located at the top of the chatter on any record. On the :guilabel:`Schedule Activity` pop-up window that appears, select an :guilabel:`Activity Type` from the drop-down menu."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:304
msgid "Individual applications have a list of *Activity Types* dedicated to that application. For example, to view and edit the activities available for the *CRM* application, go to :menuselection:`CRM app --> Configuration --> Activity Types`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:308
msgid "Enter a title for the activity in the :guilabel:`Summary` field, located in the :guilabel:`Schedule Activity` pop-up window."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:311
msgid "Select a name from the :guilabel:`Assigned to` drop-down menu to assign the activity to a different user. Otherwise, the user creating the activity is automatically assigned."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:314
msgid "Add any additional information in the optional :guilabel:`Log a note...` field."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:317
msgid "The :guilabel:`Due Date` field on the :guilabel:`Schedule Activity` pop-up window auto-populates based on the configuration settings for the selected :guilabel:`Activity Type`. However, this date can be changed by selecting a day on the calendar in the :guilabel:`Due Date` field."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:321
msgid "Lastly, click one of the following buttons:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:323
msgid ":guilabel:`Schedule`: adds the activity to the chatter under :guilabel:`Planned activities`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:324
msgid ":guilabel:`Schedule & Mark as Done`: adds the details of the activity to the chatter under :guilabel:`Today`. The activity is added to :guilabel:`Today`, and is automatically marked as done."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:327
msgid ":guilabel:`Done \\& Schedule Next`: adds the task under :guilabel:`Today` marked as done, and opens a new activity window."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:329
msgid ":guilabel:`Cancel`: discards any changes made on the pop-up window."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:331
msgid "Scheduled activities are added to the chatter for the record under :guilabel:`Planned activities`, and are color-coded based on their due date."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:334
msgid "**Red** icons indicate an overdue activity."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:335
msgid "**Yellow** icons indicate an activity with a due date scheduled for the current date."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:336
msgid "**Green** icons indicate an activity with a due date scheduled in the future."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:346
msgid "Click the :icon:`fa-info-circle` :guilabel:`(info)` icon next to a planned activity to see additional details."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:356
msgid "After completing an activity, click :guilabel:`Mark Done` under the activity entry in the chatter. This opens a :guilabel:`Mark Done` pop-up window, where additional notes about the activity can be entered. After adding any comments to the pop-up window, click: :guilabel:`Done \\& Schedule Next`, :guilabel:`Done`, or :guilabel:`Discard`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:361
msgid "After the activity is marked complete, an entry with the activity type, title, and any other details that were included in the pop-up window are listed in the chatter."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:373
msgid "Attach files"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:375
msgid "Files can be added as attachments in the chatter, either to send with messages, or to include with a record."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:379
msgid "After a file has been added to a chatter thread, it can be downloaded by any user with access to the thread. Click the |paperclip| to make the files header visible, if necessary. Then, click the :icon:`fa-download` :guilabel:`(download)` icon the file to download it."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:383
msgid "To attach a file, click the |paperclip| located at the top of the chatter composer of any record that contains a chatter thread."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:386
msgid "This opens a file explorer pop-up window. Navigate to the desired file, select it, then click :guilabel:`Open` to add it to the record. Alternatively, files can be dragged and dropped directly onto a chatter thread."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:390
msgid "After files have been added, they are listed in the chatter thread, under a :guilabel:`Files` heading."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:394
msgid "After at least one file has been added to a chatter record, a new button labeled :guilabel:`Attach files` appears below the :guilabel:`Files` heading. To attach any additional files, this is the button that **must** be used, instead of the |paperclip| at the top of the chatter thread."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:399
msgid "After the :guilabel:`Files` section heading appears in the thread, clicking the |paperclip| no longer opens a file explorer pop-up window. Instead, clicking the |paperclip| toggles the :guilabel:`Files` section from visible to invisible in the chatter thread."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:413
#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:915
msgid "Integrations"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:415
msgid "Beyond the standard features, the *Google Translate* integration can be enabled to translate the messages of the chatter."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:419
msgid "Before it can be used, the integration **must** be configured. Step-by-step instructions can be found in :doc:`../../general/integrations/google_translate`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:423
msgid "Google Translate"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:425
msgid "*Google Translate* can be used to translate user-generated text in the Odoo chatter."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:427
msgid "To enable *Google Translate* on a database, an *API key* must first :doc:`be created <../../general/integrations/google_translate>` through the `Google API Console <https://console.developers.google.com/>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:431
msgid "After creating the API key, navigate to the :menuselection:`Settings app --> Discuss section` and paste the key in the :guilabel:`Message Translation` field. Click :guilabel:`Save` to save the changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:436
msgid "Translate a chatter message"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:438
msgid "To translate a user's text from another language, click the |ve| menu to the right of the chatter. Then, select :guilabel:`Translate`. The content translates to the language set in the :doc:`user's preferences <../../general/users/language/>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:450
msgid "Using the *Google Translate* API **requires** a current billing account with `Google <https://myaccount.google.com/>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:456
msgid "Chatter extensions"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:458
msgid "Several modules extend the standard chatter."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:461
msgid "Chatter position"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:463
msgid "Each user can choose where the chatter is displayed on form views. In :menuselection:`Preferences`, set :guilabel:`Chatter Position` to :guilabel:`Side` (next to the form) or :guilabel:`Bottom` (under the form)."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:468
msgid "Requires the *MuK Chatter* (``muk_web_chatter``) module."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:471
msgid "Email delivery tracking"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:473
msgid "When an email is sent from the chatter, its delivery status is tracked and displayed next to the message: :guilabel:`Sent`, :guilabel:`Delivered`, :guilabel:`Opened`, :guilabel:`Deferred`, :guilabel:`Bounced`, :guilabel:`Soft bounced`, :guilabel:`Rejected`, :guilabel:`Spam`, :guilabel:`Unsubscribed`, or :guilabel:`Error`. Click the status to see the tracking events of that email, including the reported error."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:479
msgid "The complete list is available to administrators in :menuselection:`Settings --> Technical --> Email --> Tracking emails` and :guilabel:`Tracking events`. In :menuselection:`Settings --> General Settings --> Discuss`, the retention of these records can be limited with the maximum age in days."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:484
msgid "Requires the *Email tracking* (``mail_tracking``) module."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:487
msgid "Reply to a specific message"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:489
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Reply` on a chatter message to open the composer with the original message quoted, so that the answer keeps its context."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:493
msgid "Requires the *Mail Message Reply* (``mail_quoted_reply``) module."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:496
msgid "Preview email attachments"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:498
msgid "Emails attached to a record as `.eml` files open directly in the file viewer, like a PDF, instead of being downloaded: the header block and the body are displayed, with the embedded images."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:502
msgid "Requires the *Mail Attachment EML Preview* (``mail_attachment_eml_preview``) module."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:505
msgid "Notify followers or not"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:507
msgid "In the full composer, the :guilabel:`Notify Followers` checkbox decides whether the message is also sent to the followers of the record, or only to the recipients explicitly listed. The same option is available when sending an invoice from the :guilabel:`Send` window of the Invoicing app."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:512
msgid "Requires the *Mail Follower Notification* (``eyssen_mail_follower_notification``) module, and, for invoices, *Mail Follower Notification - Invoicing* (``eyssen_mail_follower_notification_account``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:526
msgid "Cc and Bcc recipients"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:528
msgid "In the standard full composer, all recipients are entered in a single :guilabel:`Recipients` field. With the *Email CC and BCC* module (`mail_composer_cc_bcc`), the full composer has two additional fields, :guilabel:`Cc` and :guilabel:`Bcc`, in which contacts can be selected (or created on the fly from an email address):"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:533
msgid "the :guilabel:`Recipients` and the :guilabel:`Cc` contacts appear as such, in the *To* and *Cc* headers, in the email received by every recipient;"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:535
msgid "the :guilabel:`Bcc` contacts receive a copy of the email, but their address is not disclosed to the other recipients."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:538
msgid "The two fields are available when sending a message from the chatter of any record, and in the composers based on it (e.g., sending a quotation). They are not displayed when logging an internal note."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:542
msgid "Default values can be prepared in two places:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:544
msgid "on the company: go to :menuselection:`Settings --> Users & Companies --> Companies`, open the company, and select contacts in the :guilabel:`Default Cc` and :guilabel:`Default Bcc` fields, under :guilabel:`Email`. These contacts are pre-filled in every email composed for that company, e.g., to archive all outgoing emails in a dedicated mailbox with a default Bcc contact;"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:548
msgid "on an :doc:`email template <../../general/companies/email_template>`: in addition to the standard :guilabel:`Cc` field, a :guilabel:`Bcc` field is available in the :guilabel:`Email Configuration` tab. When the template is selected in the composer, the addresses of these two fields are matched with the existing contacts, which are then added to the :guilabel:`Cc` and :guilabel:`Bcc` fields of the composer."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:563
msgid "Archive and restore log"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:565
msgid "When a record is archived or restored, the standard chatter only keeps a trace if the :guilabel:`Active` field of the model is tracked, which is rarely the case. With the *Chatter: Log Archive/Restore* module (`eyssen_chatter_log_all_state_chnage`), a note such as *“Deco Addict” was archived.* or *“Deco Addict” was restored.* is logged in the chatter of every record that has one, with the user and the date of the operation. Models that already track the field are left unchanged, so that the operation is not logged twice."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:573
msgid "To install the module, go to :menuselection:`Settings --> eYssen ERP`, and, in the :guilabel:`General Modules` section, enable :guilabel:`Chatter: Log Archive/Restore (no duplicate with tracking)`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:579
msgid ":doc:`Discuss Channels <../discuss/team_communication/>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/chatter.rst:580
msgid ":doc:`Activities <../../essentials/activities>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/ice_servers.rst:3
msgid "Configure ICE servers with Twilio"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/ice_servers.rst:5
msgid "Odoo Discuss uses WebRTC API and peer-to-peer connections for voice and video calls. If one of the call attendees is behind a symmetric NAT, you need to configure an ICE server to establish a connection to the call attendee. To set up an ICE server, first, create a Twilio account for video calls, and then, connect that Twilio account to Odoo."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/ice_servers.rst:11
msgid "Create a Twilio account"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/ice_servers.rst:13
msgid "First, go to `Twilio <https://www.twilio.com>`_ and click :guilabel:`Sign up` to create a new Twilio account. Next, enter your name and email address, create a password, and accept Twilio's terms of service. Then, click :guilabel:`Start your free trial`. Verify your email address with Twilio, as per their instructions."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/ice_servers.rst:18
msgid "Next, enter your phone number into Twilio. Then, Twilio will send you an SMS text message containing a verification code. Enter the verification code into Twilio to verify your phone number."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/ice_servers.rst:22
msgid "After that, Twilio redirects to a welcome page. Use the following list to answer Twilio's questions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/ice_servers.rst:25
msgid "For :guilabel:`Which Twilio product are you here to use?`, select :guilabel:`Video`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/ice_servers.rst:26
msgid "For :guilabel:`What do you plan to build with Twilio?`, select :guilabel:`Other`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/ice_servers.rst:27
msgid "For :guilabel:`How do you want to build with Twilio?`, select :guilabel:`With no code at all`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/ice_servers.rst:28
msgid "For :guilabel:`What is your goal today?`, select :guilabel:`3rd party integrations`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/ice_servers.rst:None
msgid "The Twilio welcome page."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/ice_servers.rst:34
msgid "If necessary, change the billing country. Finally, click :guilabel:`Get Started with Twilio`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/ice_servers.rst:37
msgid "Locate the Twilio Account SID and Auth Token"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/ice_servers.rst:39
msgid "To locate the Account SID and Auth Token, go to the Twilio account dashboard. Then, click :guilabel:`Develop` on the sidebar. In the :guilabel:`Account Info` section, locate the :guilabel:`Account SID` and the :guilabel:`Auth Token`. Both of these are needed to connect Twilio to Odoo."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/ice_servers.rst:None
msgid "The Twilio Account SID and Auth Token can be found uner the Account Info section."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/ice_servers.rst:49
msgid "Connect Twilio to Odoo"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/ice_servers.rst:51
msgid "Open the Odoo database and go to :menuselection:`Settings --> General Settings --> Discuss`. Check the box next to :guilabel:`Use Twilio ICE servers` and enter the Twilio account's :guilabel:`Account SID` and :guilabel:`Auth Token`. Finally, click :guilabel:`Save` to apply these changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/ice_servers.rst:65
msgid "Define a list of custom ICE servers"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/ice_servers.rst:67
msgid "This step is not required for the Twilio configuration. However, if Twilio is not configured or is not working at any given moment, Odoo will fall back on the custom ICE servers list. The user must define the list of custom ICE servers."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/ice_servers.rst:71
msgid "In :menuselection:`Settings --> General Settings --> Discuss`, click the :guilabel:`ICE Servers` button under :guilabel:`Custom ICE server list`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/ice_servers.rst:81
msgid "Odoo will redirect to the :guilabel:`ICE servers` page. Here you can define your own list of ICE servers."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/ice_servers.rst:92
msgid "For on-premise instances of Odoo, the package `python3-gevent` is necessary for the Discuss module to run calls/video calls on Ubuntu (Linux) servers."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/mailbox.rst:3
msgid "Mailbox"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/mailbox.rst:5
msgid "The **Mailbox** app gathers the internal messages of the database in a single three-pane screen — sidebar, message list, and preview — so that messages can be processed like in an email client, without opening each record one by one."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/mailbox.rst:10
msgid "The app is provided by the *Mailbox* (``mailbox``) module. It works on the messages already stored in the database, so nothing has to be imported."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/mailbox.rst:14
msgid "Navigate the mailbox"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/mailbox.rst:16
msgid "Open :menuselection:`Mailbox`. The left sidebar groups the messages:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/mailbox.rst:18
msgid ":guilabel:`Inbox`: the messages addressed to the user;"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/mailbox.rst:19
msgid ":guilabel:`Marked`: the messages flagged with a :ref:`mark <mailbox/marks>`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/mailbox.rst:20
msgid ":guilabel:`Channels` and :guilabel:`Direct Messages`: the Discuss conversations;"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/mailbox.rst:21
msgid ":guilabel:`Labels`: the user's own :ref:`labels <mailbox/labels>`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/mailbox.rst:22
msgid ":guilabel:`Lost messages`: the messages whose record has been deleted or is no longer accessible."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/mailbox.rst:24
msgid "Each entry shows the number of unread messages. The middle pane lists the messages of the selected section, with their subject, author, and date; selecting one opens it in the preview pane on the right, where the message, its attachments, and the thread it belongs to are displayed, and where it can be answered directly."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/mailbox.rst:37
msgid "Work with messages"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/mailbox.rst:39
msgid "From the message list, several messages can be selected to act on them at once with the bulk toolbar: mark them as read or unread, apply a label, flag them with a mark, archive them, or delete them. Deletion is a soft delete: the message is hidden but kept, together with who deleted it and when."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/mailbox.rst:44
msgid "The reply composer offers :guilabel:`Send as e-mail` to send the answer as an email instead of an internal message, and supports :guilabel:`CC` and :guilabel:`BCC` recipients."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/mailbox.rst:50
msgid "Labels"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/mailbox.rst:52
msgid "Labels classify messages across records. Manage them in :menuselection:`Mailbox --> Settings --> Labels`: each label has a :guilabel:`Name`, a color, an optional :guilabel:`Description`, a :guilabel:`Sequence`, and, in a multi-company database, a :guilabel:`Company`. The list also shows the number of messages carrying the label."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/mailbox.rst:60
msgid "Marks"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/mailbox.rst:62
msgid "Marks are personal flags, similar to the flags of an email client. Manage them in :menuselection:`Mailbox --> Settings --> Marks`, where each mark has a :guilabel:`Name`, a color, and an icon. A mark is applied per user, so two users can flag the same message differently."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/mailbox.rst:67
msgid "Audit log"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/mailbox.rst:69
msgid ":menuselection:`Mailbox --> Settings --> Audit Log` records the actions performed on the messages (edition, deletion, restoration), with their author and date."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/mailbox.rst:75
msgid "The :guilabel:`Mailbox` category of the :ref:`access rights <access-rights/users>` gives a fine control over what a user may do:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/mailbox.rst:78
msgid ":guilabel:`User: Access Mailbox`: open the app;"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/mailbox.rst:79
msgid ":guilabel:`User: Edit Own Messages` and :guilabel:`Administrator: Edit Any Message`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/mailbox.rst:80
msgid ":guilabel:`User: Delete Own Messages` and :guilabel:`Administrator: Delete Any Message`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/mailbox.rst:81
msgid ":guilabel:`User: Move Messages` and :guilabel:`User: Manage Labels`;"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/mailbox.rst:82
msgid ":guilabel:`User: Lost Messages Visibility`: see the messages whose record is gone;"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/mailbox.rst:83
msgid ":guilabel:`User: Send as E-mail`: answer by email from the mailbox;"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/discuss/mailbox.rst:84
msgid ":guilabel:`Administrator: Mailbox`: full access."
msgstr ""

