#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:3
msgid "Sign"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:5
msgid "**eYssen Sign** allows you to send, sign, and approve documents online using electronic signatures. It provides a complete document signing solution with PDF template management, a drag-and-drop field editor, multi-party signing workflows, two-factor authentication, a full audit trail, and integrations with sales, invoicing, and HR."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:10
msgid "An **electronic signature** shows a person's agreement to the content of a document. Just like a handwritten signature, the electronic one represents a legal binding by the terms of the signed document."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:22
msgid "Validity of electronic signatures"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:24
msgid "Documents signed via the Sign app are valid electronic signatures in the European Union and the United States of America. They also meet the requirements for electronic signatures in most countries. The legal validity of electronic signatures generated by eYssen Sign depends on your country's legislation. Companies doing business abroad should also consider other countries' electronic signature laws."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:31
msgid "The information below has no legal value; it is only provided for general informational purposes. As laws governing electronic signatures rapidly evolve, we cannot guarantee that all information is up-to-date. We advise contacting a local attorney for legal advice regarding electronic signature compliance and validity."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:37
msgid "European Union"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:39
msgid "The `eIDAS regulation <http://data.europa.eu/eli/reg/2014/910/oj>`_ establishes the framework for electronic signatures in the `27 member states of the European Union <https://europa.eu/european-union/about-eu/countries_en>`_. It distinguishes three types of electronic signatures:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:44
msgid "Simple electronic signatures"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:45
msgid "Advanced electronic signatures"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:46
msgid "Qualified electronic signatures"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:48
msgid "eYssen Sign generates the first type, **simple electronic signatures**; these signatures are legally valid in the EU, as stated in the eIDAS regulation."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:51
msgid "Electronic signatures may not be automatically recognized as valid. You may need to bring supporting evidence of a signature's validity. The Sign app automatically collects supporting evidence during the signing process, such as:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:55
msgid "Email and SMS verification (if enabled)"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:56
msgid "Timestamped, IP-tracked, and geographically traceable access logs to the documents and their associated signatures"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:58
msgid "Document traceability and inalterability (any alteration made to a signed document is detected using cryptographic hash chains)"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:62
msgid "United States of America"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:64
msgid "The `ESIGN Act (Electronic Signatures in Global and National Commerce Act) <https://www.fdic.gov/regulations/compliance/manual/10/X-3.1.pdf>`_, at the interstate and international levels, and the `UETA (Uniform Electronic Transactions Act) <https://www.uniformlaws.org/committees/community-home/librarydocuments?communitykey=2c04b76c-2b7d-4399-977e-d5876ba7e034&tab=librarydocuments>`_, at the state level, provide the legal framework for electronic signatures."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:70
msgid "Overall, to be recognized as valid, electronic signatures have to meet five criteria:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:72
msgid "The signer must show a clear **intent to sign**. For example, using a mouse to draw a signature can show intent. The signer must also have the option to opt out of the electronic document."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:74
msgid "The signer must first express or imply their **consent to conduct business electronically**."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:75
msgid "**The signature must be clearly attributed**. In eYssen Sign, metadata such as the signer's IP address and geolocation is added to the signature, which can be used as supporting evidence."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:77
msgid "**The signature must be associated with the signed document**, for example, by keeping a record detailing how the signature was captured."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:79
msgid "Electronically signed documents need to be **retained and stored** by all parties involved; for example, by providing the signer either a fully-executed copy or the possibility to download a copy."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:86
msgid "Dashboard"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:88
msgid "The Sign dashboard is the first screen displayed when you open the app. It provides an at-a-glance overview of your signing activity along with quick access to your templates."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:92
msgid "Statistics"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:94
msgid "At the top of the dashboard, a set of counters displays real-time signing metrics:"
