#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:126
msgid "Creating a template"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:128
msgid "To create a new template:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:130
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Upload a PDF Template` from the dashboard, or go to :menuselection:`eYssen Sign --> Templates` and click :guilabel:`New`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:132
msgid "Select a PDF file from your computer."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:133
msgid "The template editor opens, allowing you to place signing fields on the document."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:138
msgid "Template editor"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:140
msgid "The template editor provides a visual, drag-and-drop interface for placing fields onto the pages of your PDF document."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:151
msgid "The left sidebar lists all available :ref:`field types <sign/field-types>`. Drag a field from the sidebar and drop it onto the desired location on the PDF. Once placed, you can:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:154
msgid "**Resize** the field by dragging its corners."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:155
msgid "**Move** the field to a different position on the page."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:156
msgid "**Change the role** assigned to the field by clicking on it and selecting a different role from the dropdown."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:158
msgid "**Mark as required** to force signers to fill in the field before completing their signature."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:159
msgid "**Delete** the field by selecting it and pressing the delete key or clicking the trash icon."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:161
msgid "Each field is color-coded according to the :ref:`role <sign/roles>` it is assigned to, making it easy to see which signer is responsible for which fields."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:165
msgid "Use the page navigation controls at the bottom of the editor to move between pages of a multi-page PDF document."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:169
msgid "PDF rotation"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:171
msgid "If your PDF pages are not oriented correctly, you can rotate them directly in the template editor. Click the rotation button in the toolbar to rotate the current page by 90 degrees."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:177
msgid "Template properties"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:179
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Template Properties` in the template editor to configure additional settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:188
msgid "The following properties are available:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:190
msgid ":guilabel:`Name`: the display name of the template."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:191
msgid ":guilabel:`Category`: assign a category for organizational purposes."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:192
msgid ":guilabel:`Tags`: add one or more tags for filtering and searching."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:193
msgid ":guilabel:`Redirect URL`: a URL the signer is redirected to after completing their signature. This link also appears in the signature confirmation email."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:195
msgid ":guilabel:`Authorized Users`: restrict which users can use this template. Leave empty to allow all Sign users."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:197
msgid ":guilabel:`Authorized Groups`: restrict template access to members of specific security groups."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:202
msgid "Version management"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:204
msgid "eYssen Sign tracks template versions automatically. When you need to update a template (for example, to change the PDF or modify field placement), you can create a new version instead of editing the current one. This preserves the integrity of existing signing requests that reference earlier versions."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:209
msgid "To create a new version:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:211
msgid "Open the template and click :guilabel:`Create New Version`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:212
msgid "Upload the updated PDF or make changes to the field layout."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:213
msgid "Save the new version. The previous version is automatically archived."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:215
msgid "Existing signing requests continue to reference the version of the template that was current when they were created."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:219
msgid "Version comparison"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:221
msgid "You can compare two versions of a template side by side to see what changed. Open a template and click :guilabel:`Compare Versions`. The comparison view highlights:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:224
msgid "**Added fields**: fields present in the new version but not in the old one (shown in green)."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:225
msgid "**Removed fields**: fields present in the old version but not in the new one (shown in red)."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:226
msgid "**Modified fields**: fields whose position, size, or properties changed between versions (shown in yellow)."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:239
msgid "Multilingual support"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:241
msgid "eYssen Sign supports two approaches for handling documents in multiple languages:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:243
msgid "**Mode A: Template Copy per Language**"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:245
msgid "Create a separate PDF document for each language. Each copy is linked to the parent template and associated with a specific language. When sending a request, the system selects the appropriate language copy based on the recipient's preferred language."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:249
#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:261
msgid "To set up:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:251
msgid "Open the template and set :guilabel:`Multilingual Mode` to :guilabel:`Template Copy per Language`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:253
msgid "Create child template copies for each language by clicking :guilabel:`Create Language Copy`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:254
msgid "Upload the localized PDF and configure the fields for each copy."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:256
msgid "**Mode B: Dynamic Field Translation**"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:258
msgid "Use Odoo's built-in translation system to translate field default values and placeholder text. The PDF itself remains the same, but text fields are populated in the signer's language."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:263
msgid "Open the template and set :guilabel:`Multilingual Mode` to :guilabel:`Dynamic Field Translation`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:265
msgid "Switch to the desired language using the language selector and translate the default values of text fields."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:269
msgid "Mode B works best for templates where the PDF content is language-neutral (e.g., forms with labeled boxes) and only the field values need translation."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:275
msgid "Favorites"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:277
msgid "Star a template to mark it as a favorite. Favorite templates appear first on the dashboard. Click the star icon on a template card or inside the template form view to toggle the favorite status."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:283
msgid "Share link"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:285
msgid "Generate a public URL that allows anyone to sign a document without requiring an Odoo account."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:295
msgid "To generate a share link:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:297
msgid "Open the template."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:298
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Share`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:299
msgid "Copy the generated URL and distribute it via email, chat, or any other channel."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:301
msgid "When someone opens the link, they can fill in their details and sign the document. A new signing request is automatically created for each person who signs via the shared link."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:305
msgid "Share links can be deactivated at any time by clicking :guilabel:`Disable Link` on the template."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:310
msgid "Roles"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:312
msgid "Each field in a Sign document is assigned to a **role** that corresponds to a specific signer. When a document is sent for signing, each role is mapped to a person who must fill in the fields assigned to their role."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:316
msgid "In the template editor, select a field and pick its :guilabel:`Role` in the properties panel on the right. Each role has:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:319
msgid "a name (e.g., *Customer*, *Employee*, *Witness*);"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:320
msgid "a color, used to visually distinguish the fields belonging to that role in the editor;"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:321
msgid "a sequence, determining the default order when several roles exist;"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:322
msgid "an authentication method, applied to the signer filling that role."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:325
msgid "The set of roles is part of the app's configuration data and is maintained by the administrator."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:330
msgid "Field types"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:332
msgid "Fields define the type of information signers must provide. The following field types are available:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:334
msgid ":guilabel:`Signature`: the signer draws, auto-generates, or uploads their signature. Subsequent signature fields automatically reuse the first signature entered."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:336
msgid ":guilabel:`Initials`: similar to signature, but for the signer's initials."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:337
msgid ":guilabel:`Text`: a single-line text input."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:338
msgid ":guilabel:`Multiline Text`: a multi-line text area for longer content."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:339
msgid ":guilabel:`Checkbox`: a tick box (e.g., for consent or approval)."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:340
msgid ":guilabel:`Selection`: a dropdown allowing the signer to choose one option from a predefined list."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:341
msgid ":guilabel:`Date`: a date picker field."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:343
msgid "Field types, including their tip, placeholder, and the partner field used for :ref:`auto-fill <sign/auto-fill>`, are part of the app's configuration data and are maintained by the administrator."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:350
msgid "Auto-fill from partner data"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:352
msgid "Each field type can be configured with an :guilabel:`Auto-fill Partner Field` that automatically populates the field with data from the signer's contact record (``res.partner``). For example, setting the auto-fill field to ``email`` pre-fills the field with the signer's email address."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:357
msgid "To find the technical name of a contact field, enable developer mode and hover over the question mark icon next to the field on the contact form."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:361
msgid "Auto-filled values are suggestions only. The signer can modify them before completing the signature."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:365
msgid "Field sizing"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:367
msgid "The size of fields can be adjusted by editing the :guilabel:`Default Width` and :guilabel:`Default Height`. Both values are expressed as a percentage of the full page (decimal format), where ``1`` equals the full page width or height. For example, ``0.150`` means 15% of the page width."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:374
msgid "Sign requests"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:376
msgid "A sign request represents a specific document sent to one or more signers for their signature. Go to :menuselection:`eYssen Sign --> Sign Requests` to view all signing requests."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:387
msgid "Creating a request"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:389
msgid "To create a new signing request:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:391
msgid "From the dashboard, click :guilabel:`Send` on a template card. Alternatively, go to :menuselection:`eYssen Sign --> Sign Requests` and click :guilabel:`New`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:393
msgid "Select the template to use."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:394
msgid "In the send wizard, assign a contact to each role defined in the template."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:405
msgid "Signing order"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:407
msgid "Choose how signers receive the document:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:409
msgid ":guilabel:`Parallel`: all signers receive the document simultaneously and can sign in any order."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:410
msgid ":guilabel:`Sequential`: signers receive the document one at a time, in the order you define. Each signer receives the document only after the previous one has completed their part."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:413
msgid "For sequential signing, set the order number for each signer in the send wizard."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:418
msgid "State machine"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:420
msgid "Every sign request follows a defined lifecycle:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:422
msgid "**Draft**: the request has been created but not yet sent."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:423
msgid "**Sent**: the request has been sent to the signers."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:424
msgid "**Signed**: all signers have completed their signatures."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:425
msgid "**Refused**: one or more signers refused to sign the document."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:426
msgid "**Canceled**: the request was canceled by the creator."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:427
msgid "**Expired**: the request's expiry date has passed without all signatures being collected."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:430
msgid "Terminal states (*Signed*, *Refused*, *Canceled*, *Expired*) cannot be reversed. This ensures the integrity of the audit trail."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:436
msgid "Two-factor authentication (2FA)"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:438
msgid "For additional security, you can require signers to verify their identity with a one-time password (OTP) before completing their signature."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:447
msgid "To enable 2FA on a request:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:449
msgid "In the send wizard, enable :guilabel:`Require 2FA`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:450
msgid "Select the verification method:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:452
msgid ":guilabel:`Email`: a 6-digit code is sent to the signer's email address."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:453
msgid ":guilabel:`SMS`: a 6-digit code is sent via SMS to the signer's mobile number."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:454
msgid ":guilabel:`Email & SMS`: codes are sent via both channels; both must be verified."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:456
msgid "The OTP code is valid for **10 minutes**. The signer has **3 attempts** to enter the correct code. After 3 failed attempts, a **15-minute lockout** period is enforced before a new code can be requested."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:461
msgid "SMS verification sends the code through the database's SMS service, which requires SMS credits."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:465
msgid "Expiry date"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:467
msgid "Set an expiry date on a request to enforce a deadline. If all signatures are not collected by the expiry date, the request automatically moves to the *Expired* state. A scheduled action (cron job) runs periodically to check and expire overdue requests."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:474
msgid "Enable automatic reminders to nudge signers who have not yet completed their part. In the send wizard, set the :guilabel:`Reminder Frequency` (in days). The system sends periodic email reminders to pending signers at the specified interval."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:479
msgid "Escalation"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:481
msgid "Set an :guilabel:`Escalation Before Expiry` value (in days) to notify the request creator a specified number of days before the expiry date. This gives the creator time to follow up with pending signers or extend the deadline."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:486
msgid "Language selection"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:488
msgid "Select a :guilabel:`Language` on the request to control the language used in email notifications sent to signers. If the template uses the *Template Copy per Language* multilingual mode, the matching language copy of the template is used automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:493
msgid "Cancel and refuse"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:495
msgid "**Cancel**: the request creator can cancel a request at any time while it is in the *Sent* state. All pending signers are notified of the cancellation."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:497
msgid "**Refuse**: any signer can refuse to sign. The request moves to the *Refused* state, and all participants (including the creator) are notified."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:503
msgid "Signing portal"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:505
msgid "The signing portal is the public-facing interface where signers review and sign documents. It is accessible at ``/sign/<token>``, where ``<token>`` is a unique, secure access token generated for each signer."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:517
msgid "PDF viewer"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:519
msgid "The signing portal displays the PDF document with interactive fields highlighted for the current signer. Fields belonging to the signer's role are editable; fields assigned to other roles are visible but read-only."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:524
msgid "Signature capture"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:526
msgid "When the signer reaches a signature or initials field, they can:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:528
msgid "**Draw**: use the mouse or a touchscreen to draw their signature."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:529
msgid "**Auto-generate**: the system generates a signature based on the signer's name."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:530
msgid "**Upload**: upload an image file containing the signature."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:532
msgid "If the signer has previously saved a signature on their partner record, it is offered as a quick-select option for reuse."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:543
msgid "OTP verification step"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:545
msgid "If 2FA is enabled on the request, the signer is prompted to enter a one-time verification code before their signature is finalized. See :ref:`sign/2fa` for details on the verification process."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:549
msgid "Refuse option"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:551
msgid "Signers can refuse to sign by clicking :guilabel:`Refuse to Sign`. A notification is sent to the request creator and all other participants. The request moves to the *Refused* state."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:555
msgid "Redirect after signing"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:557
msgid "If a :guilabel:`Redirect URL` is configured on the template, the signer is redirected to that URL after successfully completing their signature."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:561
msgid "Terms & conditions"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:563
msgid "If the company has configured Terms & Conditions in the Sign settings, they are displayed to the signer before they finalize their signature. The signer must accept the terms to proceed."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:567
msgid "Geolocation capture"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:569
msgid "With the signer's consent, the portal captures the signer's geographic location (latitude and longitude) at the time of signing. This data is recorded in the audit log as additional evidence of the signing event."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:574
msgid "QR code"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:576
msgid "A QR code can be generated for a signing URL, allowing signers to quickly access the signing portal on a mobile device by scanning the code."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:588
msgid "Portal — My Signatures"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:590
msgid "Signers who have an Odoo portal account can access a list of all their signing requests at ``/my/sign``."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:600
msgid "The portal page displays:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:602
msgid "**Reference**: the name of the signing request."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:603
msgid "**Status**: the current state of the request (*Sent*, *Signed*, *Refused*, etc.)."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:604
msgid "**Date**: when the request was created."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:605
msgid "**Download**: a link to download the completed signed PDF (available once fully signed)."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:610
msgid "Workflows"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:612
msgid "The workflow engine allows you to define complex signing and approval processes using a visual graph builder. Go to :menuselection:`eYssen Sign --> Workflows` to manage workflows."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:623
msgid "Creating a workflow"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:625
msgid "Click :guilabel:`New` to create a new workflow."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:626
msgid "Enter a :guilabel:`Name` and optionally link a default :guilabel:`Sign Template`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:627
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Open Builder` to launch the visual workflow builder."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:630
msgid "Node types"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:632
msgid "The following node types are available:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:634
msgid ":guilabel:`Start`: the entry point of the workflow. Each workflow can have at most one Start node."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:635
msgid ":guilabel:`Signature`: a signing step. Assign a role to define which signer must act at this step."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/sign.rst:636
msgid ":guilabel:`Approval`: an approval step that does not require a signature but requires explicit approval from the assigned role."
msgstr ""

