msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/utilities.rst:28
msgid "The *Web Gantt* (``web_gantt``) module adds a Gantt view type: on models that have a start and a stop date, records are displayed as bars on a timeline, which can be zoomed and scrolled. Where the view is available, it appears in the view switcher of the model, next to the list and kanban views, and it can also be added to :doc:`My Dashboard <dashboards/my_dashboard>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/utilities.rst:34
msgid "The Gantt view has to be declared on a model; it is not automatically available everywhere."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/whatsapp.rst:3
msgid "WhatsApp"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/whatsapp.rst:5
msgid "The **Odoo WhatsApp Connector** (``whatsapp_mail_messaging``) lets users send quotations, invoices, and portal links to customers through **WhatsApp Web** or the WhatsApp mobile app. Odoo does not connect to the WhatsApp Business API: it prepares the message text and opens WhatsApp with the recipient and the message already filled in, so the message is sent from the user's own WhatsApp account."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/whatsapp.rst:12
msgid "The module requires the *Sales*, *Invoicing*, and *Website* apps. Every recipient must have a :guilabel:`Mobile` number on their contact record, in international format."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/whatsapp.rst:19
msgid "Message template"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/whatsapp.rst:21
msgid "To define the text proposed by default when sending a quotation or an invoice, go to :menuselection:`Settings --> General Settings`, scroll to the :guilabel:`Whatsapp` section, and fill in the :guilabel:`Message Template` field. The template is stored per company; if it is left empty, Odoo composes a default message containing the customer name, the document number, and the total amount."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/whatsapp.rst:36
msgid "Website chat button"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/whatsapp.rst:38
msgid "The module adds a WhatsApp icon to the social media area of the website footer. Visitors can use it to start a chat with the company. For the icon to work, enter the company's WhatsApp number in the :guilabel:`Mobile Number` field of the website record (:menuselection:`Website --> Configuration --> Settings`, then open the website form)."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/whatsapp.rst:43
msgid "The messages offered to visitors in the chat window are managed in :menuselection:`Website --> Configuration --> Whatsapp Messages`. Each record has a :guilabel:`Name` and a :guilabel:`Message`; visitors can select one of them or choose :guilabel:`Custom` and type their own text."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/whatsapp.rst:55
msgid "Send a quotation or an invoice"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/whatsapp.rst:57
msgid "Open a quotation or an invoice and click the :guilabel:`Send by Whatsapp` button next to the standard send buttons. A :guilabel:`Compose Whatsapp Message` window opens with:"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/whatsapp.rst:60
msgid ":guilabel:`Recipient`: the customer of the document;"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/whatsapp.rst:61
msgid ":guilabel:`Contact Number`: the mobile number of the recipient (editable);"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/whatsapp.rst:62
msgid ":guilabel:`Message`: the message template, or the generated default text."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/whatsapp.rst:64
msgid "Click :guilabel:`Send Message` to open WhatsApp with the message prepared. The text is also logged in the recipient's chatter."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/whatsapp.rst:67
msgid "Several documents can be sent at once: select them in the list view and click :guilabel:`Send by Whatsapp`. All selected documents must belong to the same customer; otherwise, Odoo raises an error."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/whatsapp.rst:79
msgid "Share a portal link"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/whatsapp.rst:81
msgid "When sharing a record with a customer (the :guilabel:`Share` action that opens the portal share window), a :guilabel:`Sharing Method` field allows :guilabel:`Whatsapp` to be selected instead of :guilabel:`Mail`. Select the :guilabel:`Customer`, check the :guilabel:`Mobile number`, and send: the portal link and the note are sent through WhatsApp and logged in the record's chatter."
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/whatsapp.rst:87
msgid "Systray shortcuts"
msgstr ""

#: ../mnt/documentation/content/applications/productivity/whatsapp.rst:89
msgid "Two icons are added to the top-right systray area: one opens the :guilabel:`Compose Whatsapp Message` window for any number, the other opens a blank email composition form."
msgstr ""
